{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018fRp4YMdJsJHZxCdWo3Ujd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Area 15: packaging, build, tooling, release, cutover\n2\t\n3\t## 1. Purpose\n4\t\n5\tThis area defines how Roast is built, tested, linted, checked, released, and\n6\tshipped as one pure-JS npm package, `@substrate-system/roast`. It replaces\n7\tthe Go toolchain, the six platform packages, the npm launcher, and the\n8\tplatform release scripts. It also defines two milestones: the M0 scaffold\n9\t(tooling that lets the other areas land code and tests) and the M6 cutover\n10\t(deleting the Go implementation and releasing `2.0.0`).\n11\t\n12\tVocabulary: \"the bundle\" is `dist/cli.js`, the single esbuild ESM output\n13\tthat `bin.roast` points at. \"Third-party notices\" is\n14\t`dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`. \"The test bundle\" is\n15\t`test/test-bundle.js`, the esbuild output of `test/index.ts`. \"The\n16\tbaseline\" is Go commit `cd08f10`.\n17\t\n18\tUsers install Roast as a project dependency\n19\t(`npm i -D @substrate-system/roast`) and run it as `npx roast ...`; it is\n20\tnever a `PATH` binary. Installing it adds no transitive packages.\n21\t\n22\t## 2. Behavior contract\n23\t\n24\tThis section is the build and release contract, not CLI behavior.\n25\t\n26\t### 2.1 Package manifest (final form, after M6)\n27\t\n28\t`package.json` at the repo root, exactly these keys (key order is not\n29\tsignificant; values are):\n30\t\n31\t```json\n32\t{\n33\t  \"name\": \"@substrate-system/roast\",\n34\t  \"version\": \"2.0.0\",\n35\t  \"description\": \"Adversarial review\",\n36\t  \"license\": \"(MIT OR Apache-2.0)\",\n37\t  \"type\": \"module\",\n38\t  \"bin\": {\n39\t    \"roast\": \"dist/cli.js\"\n40\t  },\n41\t  \"files\": [\n42\t    \"dist/cli.js\",\n43\t    \"dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt\",\n44\t    \"roast.schema.json\",\n45\t    \"LICENSE.txt\",\n46\t    \"LICENSE-MIT.txt\",\n47\t    \"LICENSE-APACHE.txt\"\n48\t  ],\n49\t  \"engines\": {\n50\t    \"node\": \">=22.18\"\n51\t  },\n52\t  \"os\": [\"darwin\", \"linux\"],\n53\t  \"publishConfig\": {\n54\t    \"access\": \"public\"\n55\t  },\n56\t  \"scripts\": {\n57\t    \"lint\": \"eslint src test scripts eslint.config.js\",\n58\t    \"typecheck\": \"tsc -p tsconfig.json\",\n59\t    \"schema\": \"node scripts/schema.ts\",\n60\t    \"build\": \"npm run schema && node scripts/bundle.ts\",\n61\t    \"build:test\": \"node scripts/bundle.ts --test\",\n62\t    \"test\": \"npm run build && npm run test:run\",\n63\t    \"test:run\": \"npm run build:test && npm run test:tap\",\n64\t    \"test:tap\": \"bash -o pipefail -c 'node test/test-bundle.js | tap-spec'\",\n65\t    \"test:live\": \"node scripts/bundle.ts --live && node test/live-bundle.js\",\n66\t    \"check:pack\": \"node scripts/check-pack.ts\",\n67\t    \"toc\": \"markdown-toc --maxdepth 3 -i README.md\",\n68\t    \"preversion\": \"npm run lint\",\n69\t    \"version\": \"npm run toc && auto-changelog && npm run stage:docs\",\n70\t    \"stage:docs\": \"git add CHANGELOG.md README.md\",\n71\t    \"postversion\": \"git push --follow-tags && npm publish\",\n72\t    \"prepublishOnly\": \"npm run build && npm run check:pack\"\n73\t  },\n74\t  \"auto-changelog\": {\n75\t    \"package\": true,\n76\t    \"template\": \"keepachangelog\",\n77\t    \"breakingPattern\": \"BREAKING CHANGE:\"\n78\t  },\n79\t  \"devDependencies\": {\n80\t    \"@substrate-system/debug\": \"^0.9.64\",\n81\t    \"@substrate-system/redeye\": \"^0.1.7\",\n82\t    \"@substrate-system/tapzero\": \"^0.10.15\",\n83\t    \"@types/node\": \"^22.18.0\",\n84\t    \"@types/yargs\": \"^17.0.33\",\n85\t    \"auto-changelog\": \"^2.4.0\",\n86\t    \"esbuild\": \"^0.27.0\",\n87\t    \"eslint\": \"^10.6.0\",\n88\t    \"jsonc-parser\": \"^3.3.1\",\n89\t    \"markdown-toc\": \"^1.2.0\",\n90\t    \"newneostandard\": \"^0.14.1\",\n91\t    \"tap-spec\": \"^5.0.0\",\n92\t    \"typescript\": \"^7.0.2\",\n93\t    \"typescript-eslint\": \"^8.62.0\",\n94\t    \"yargs\": \"^18.2.0\",\n95\t    \"zod\": \"^4.6.7\"\n96\t  },\n97\t  \"keywords\": [\"AI\"],\n98\t  \"homepage\": \"https://github.com/nichoth/roast#readme\",\n99\t  \"bugs\": { \"url\": \"https://github.com/nichoth/roast/issues\" },\n100\t  \"repository\": {\n101\t    \"type\": \"git\",\n102\t    \"url\": \"git+https://github.com/nichoth/roast.git\"\n103\t  },\n104\t  \"author\": \"nichoth\"\n105\t}\n106\t```\n107\t\n108\tRules the manifest must keep:\n109\t\n110\t1. No `dependencies`, `optionalDependencies`, `peerDependencies`, or\n111\t   `workspaces`. The runtime libraries (`yargs`, `zod`, `jsonc-parser`,\n112\t   `@substrate-system/debug`) are `devDependencies` and bundled into\n113\t   `dist/cli.js`. Anything in `dependencies` would install into every\n114\t   user's project. (The working tree at the time of writing moved\n115\t   `jsonc-parser`, `yargs`, `zod` into `dependencies`; that is wrong for\n116\t   the TS package and must be reverted to `devDependencies`.)\n117\t2. No `main` or `exports`. Roast is CLI only; importing the package fails.\n118\t3. `files` lists exact paths, so `dist/meta.json` (the esbuild metafile)\n119\t   and any other build by-product never ship.\n120\t4. `roast.schema.json` stays at the package root. `roast init` writes a\n121\t   `$schema` of `node_modules/@substrate-system/roast/roast.schema.json`\n122\t   (see the init area), so the package name and this path are a contract.\n123\t5. `os` makes npm refuse the install on Windows (EBADPLATFORM).\n124\t6. `engines.node` `>=22.18` is the floor because Node 22.18 runs `.ts`\n125\t   files with type stripping unflagged (the `scripts/*.ts` tooling relies\n126\t   on it) and `node:zlib` has zstd from 22.15.\n127\t7. `devEngines` (present at the baseline) is removed: `engines` now states\n128\t   the same floor.\n129\t8. `@types/node` tracks the engine floor's major (22), so code cannot\n130\t   typecheck against an API newer than the minimum supported Node.\n131\t9. `version` is `2.0.0` only after the M6 release; during M0 to M5 it stays\n132\t   whatever the baseline has (`0.0.0`).\n133\t\n134\tThe `auto-changelog` options live in the `\"auto-changelog\"` key\n135\t(auto-changelog reads it from `package.json`) and the `git add` is split\n136\tinto `stage:docs`, so every script fits in 80 columns.\n137\t\n138\t`CHANGELOG.md` keeps its existing history (the upstream 1.4.x entries\n139\tstay as committed). From `2.0.0` on, `auto-changelog` regenerates the\n140\tnew entries from git tags at each `npm version`.\n141\t\n142\t`@types/yargs` is a `devDependency` because yargs 18 does not ship its\n143\town types.\n144\t\n145\t### 2.2 npm config and ignores\n146\t\n147\t`.npmrc` (final form) is the template's single line:\n148\t\n149\t```\n150\tpackage-lock=false\n151\t```\n152\t\n153\tThe baseline's `force=true` existed only so npm would link the\n154\t`os`/`cpu`-restricted workspaces; it is removed at M6 together with\n155\t`packages/`. There is still no committed lockfile.\n156\t\n157\t`.gitignore` gains `test/*.js` (the test bundles). At M6 it drops the\n158\tGo-era entries `/bin/`, `/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/`, `*.test`, `/roast`,\n159\t`/roast.exe`. `dist/` stays ignored.\n160\t\n161\tNo `.npmignore`: the `files` allowlist governs the tarball.\n162\t\n163\t### 2.3 TypeScript config\n164\t\n165\t`tsconfig.json` (typecheck only; esbuild does all emitting):\n166\t\n167\t```json\n168\t{\n169\t  \"compilerOptions\": {\n170\t    \"module\": \"ES2022\",\n171\t    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n172\t    \"moduleResolution\": \"Bundler\",\n173\t    \"lib\": [\"ES2022\"],\n174\t    \"types\": [\"node\"],\n175\t    \"allowJs\": false,\n176\t    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n177\t    \"strict\": true,\n178\t    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n179\t    \"forceConsistentCasingInFileNames\": true,\n180\t    \"resolveJsonModule\": true,\n181\t    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n182\t    \"noEmit\": true\n183\t  },\n184\t  \"include\": [\"src\", \"test\", \"scripts\"]\n185\t}\n186\t```\n187\t\n188\t`tsconfig.build.json` (passed to esbuild as `tsconfig` for the bundle):\n189\t\n190\t```json\n191\t{\n192\t  \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.json\",\n193\t  \"exclude\": [\"test\", \"scripts\"]\n194\t}\n195\t```\n196\t\n197\tDifferences from `../template-ts-browser/tsconfig.json` and why:\n198\t\n199\t- `lib` has no `DOM` or `WebWorker`; `types` is `[\"node\"]`, not\n200\t  `vite/client`. `fetch`, `AbortSignal`, `TextDecoder`, and\n201\t  `ReadableStream` come from `@types/node`.\n202\t- `noImplicitAny: false` is dropped, so `strict` is fully on.\n203\t- `experimentalDecorators`, `emitDecoratorMetadata`, `declaration*`,\n204\t  `sourceMap`, `outDir`, `listFiles` are dropped: no decorators, no\n205\t  library output, no tsc emit.\n206\t- `allowImportingTsExtensions` plus `noEmit`: `scripts/*.ts` run directly\n207\t  under Node type stripping, which requires `.ts` in relative imports.\n208\t  Code under `src/` and `test/` imports siblings with the `.js` extension\n209\t  (template style); `Bundler` resolution maps it to the `.ts` file.\n210\t- `include` drops `example` and `lib.es5.d.ts`, adds `scripts`.\n211\t\n212\tNode-run scripts (`scripts/*.ts`) may use only erasable TypeScript syntax:\n213\tno `enum`, `namespace`, parameter properties, or decorators. Type-only\n214\timports must use `import type`.\n215\t\n216\tAmbient declarations in `src/assets.d.ts`:\n217\t\n218\t```ts\n219\tdeclare module '*.tmpl' {\n220\t    const text:string\n221\t    export default text\n222\t}\n223\tdeclare module '*.md' {\n224\t    const text:string\n225\t    export default text\n226\t}\n227\tdeclare module '*.sh' {\n228\t    const text:string\n229\t    export default text\n230\t}\n231\tdeclare const __ROAST_VERSION__:string|undefined\n232\tdeclare const __ROAST_COMMIT__:string|undefined\n233\tdeclare const __ROAST_DATE__:string|undefined\n234\t```\n235\t\n236\t### 2.4 Lint\n237\t\n238\t`eslint.config.js` is copied from `../template-ts-browser/eslint.config.js`\n239\tbyte for byte: the `newneostandard({ ts: true })` base, the Standard Style\n240\toverrides, the `@typescript-eslint/recommended` block, and the local\n241\t`union-spacing` rule. Its rules are not changed. Its `ignores` array is\n242\tkept as is (`lib.es5.d.ts`, `dist/**`, `public/**`, `test/*.js`); the\n243\tentries that do not match anything in Roast are harmless.\n244\t\n245\tThe `lint` script names directories (`src test scripts eslint.config.js`)\n246\tinstead of the template's `./**/*.{ts,js}`, because flat-config eslint\n247\tdoes not skip dot-directories such as `.scratch/` and `.claude/`.\n248\t\n249\tConsequences the code must respect (from those rules): 4-space indent, no\n250\tsemicolons, single quotes, `name:Type` with no spaces around the colon,\n251\tobject literal members as `{ a:1 }` (`key-spacing` with `afterColon:\n252\tfalse`), `A|B` unions with no spaces, `import type` for type-only imports,\n253\tunused variables only with a `_` prefix.\n254\t\n255\tDuring M0 to M5 the legacy files do not follow these rules (they use\n256\t`{ cwd: ROOT }` spacing). The transitional `lint` script adds\n257\t`--ignore-pattern` flags for them instead of editing the config; see 2.14.\n258\t\n259\t### 2.5 The bundle (`scripts/bundle.ts`)\n260\t\n261\t`npm run build` runs `npm run schema` (2.7), then `node scripts/bundle.ts`,\n262\twhich:\n263\t\n264\t1. Removes and recreates `dist/`.\n265\t2. Calls `esbuild.build` with the options below.\n266\t3. Writes the metafile to `dist/meta.json`.\n267\t4. Writes `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt` from the metafile (2.6).\n268\t5. `chmod 0o755 dist/cli.js`. npm sets the bin mode on install, but links\n269\t   it does not refresh (an existing npx cache entry, `npx roast` inside\n270\t   this repo) need the file executable already.\n271\t6. Exits non-zero on any esbuild error or notice-generation error. Esbuild\n272\t   warnings are printed and do not fail the build.\n273\t\n274\tEsbuild options for the bundle:\n275\t\n276\t```ts\n277\tconst options:BuildOptions = {\n278\t    entryPoints: ['src/cli.ts'],\n279\t    outfile: 'dist/cli.js',\n280\t    bundle: true,\n281\t    platform: 'node',\n282\t    format: 'esm',\n283\t    target: 'node22',\n284\t    tsconfig: 'tsconfig.build.json',\n285\t    mainFields: ['module', 'main'],\n286\t    keepNames: true,\n287\t    minify: false,\n288\t    sourcemap: false,\n289\t    metafile: true,\n290\t    loader: { '.tmpl': 'text', '.md': 'text', '.sh': 'text' },\n291\t    banner: { js: BANNER },\n292\t    define: {\n293\t        __ROAST_VERSION__: JSON.stringify(version),\n294\t        __ROAST_COMMIT__: JSON.stringify(commit),\n295\t        __ROAST_DATE__: JSON.stringify(date),\n296\t    },\n297\t    logLevel: 'warning',\n298\t}\n299\t```\n300\t\n301\tWhere:\n302\t\n303\t- `BANNER` is three lines: `#!/usr/bin/env node`, then\n304\t  `import { createRequire as __roastRequire } from 'node:module'`, then\n305\t  `const require = __roastRequire(import.meta.url)`. The shebang must be\n306\t  the first line of the file. The `require` shim exists because esbuild's\n307\t  ESM output turns a bundled CommonJS module's `require('node:fs')` into a\n308\t  runtime \"Dynamic require is not supported\" error unless a `require` is\n309\t  in scope.\n310\t- `mainFields: ['module', 'main']` overrides esbuild's Node default\n311\t  (`main` first). `jsonc-parser`'s `main` is a UMD build whose internal\n312\t  `require` calls esbuild cannot follow; its `module` field is the ESM\n313\t  build.\n314\t- `version` is the root `package.json` `version`. `commit` is\n315\t  `git rev-parse --short=7 HEAD` and `date` is `git log -1 --format=%cI`\n316\t  (committer date, RFC 3339), both run at the repo root. If either `git`\n317\t  call fails (a build from a tarball), the value is `unknown`. These are\n318\t  the same three values the Go build stamped through `-ldflags -X`.\n319\t- `minify: false` and `keepNames: true` keep user-reported stack traces\n320\t  readable. `legalComments` keeps esbuild's bundle default (`eof`).\n321\t\n322\tThe yargs locale caveat. yargs loads translations with `y18n` from a\n323\t`locales/` directory next to its own module file. In the bundle that\n324\tdirectory does not exist. y18n treats a missing locale file as an empty\n325\ttable and returns the English source strings, so help and error text stay\n326\tEnglish. The CLI must still call `.locale('en')` and `.detectLocale(false)`\n327\tso yargs never tries to read `LANG`/`LC_ALL` and no locale file is ever\n328\tprobed. A bundle smoke test (5.1) proves output is identical under a\n329\tnon-English locale. If a future yargs version throws on the missing\n330\tdirectory, the fix is in the bundle step (copy nothing; pass an explicit\n331\t`y18n` instance or stub), never shipping `locales/`.\n332\t\n333\tText assets. Prompt templates, the agent skill `SKILL.md`, and the\n334\tpre-commit hook script are imported as strings through the text loader\n335\t(`import finderCore from './templates/finder_core.tmpl'`). The string must\n336\tequal the file's bytes decoded as UTF-8; none of these files has a BOM.\n337\tLocation of the files:\n338\t\n339\t- prompt templates (the 12 `*.tmpl` files): `internal/prompts/templates/`\n340\t  during M1 to M5, `src/prompts/templates/` after M6;\n341\t- agent skill: `internal/skill/assets/roast/SKILL.md`, then\n342\t  `src/skill/assets/roast/SKILL.md`;\n343\t- hook script: `internal/gate/pre-commit.sh`, then\n344\t  `src/gate/pre-commit.sh`.\n345\t\n346\tUntil M6 the TS modules import the assets from their Go locations, so the\n347\tGo `//go:embed` directives and the TS bundle read the same file and cannot\n348\tdrift. M6 moves them with `git mv` and updates the import paths. Go embeds\n349\t`all:assets/roast` as a directory; the TS skill module imports each file\n350\texplicitly, so a new file under `assets/roast/` needs a new import.\n351\t\n352\t`npx roast` inside this repository resolves the root package's own `bin`.\n353\tBuild first: with no `dist/cli.js`, a `roast` elsewhere on `PATH` (for\n354\texample Homebrew) can answer instead.\n355\t\n356\t### 2.6 Third-party notices (`scripts/licenses.ts`)\n357\t\n358\tGenerated by the bundle step from the in-memory metafile. Algorithm:\n359\t\n360\t1. Take `metafile.outputs['dist/cli.js'].inputs`. Keep only input paths\n361\t   with `bytesInOutput > 0` (code actually in the bundle) that contain a\n362\t   `node_modules/` segment.\n363\t2. For each path, the package root is the prefix up to and including the\n364\t   package name after the last `node_modules/`: one segment, or two when\n365\t   the first starts with `@` (scoped). Nested `node_modules` resolve to\n366\t   the innermost package.\n367\t3. Read `<root>/package.json`: `name`, `version`, `license` (a string; the\n368\t   legacy object or array `licenses` form is an error), and `repository`\n369\t   (string or `{ url }`, optional).\n370\t4. License files are the files directly in `<root>` whose name matches\n371\t   `/^(licen[cs]e|copying|notice)(\\..*)?$/i`, sorted by name.\n372\t5. Deduplicate by `name@version`.\n373\t6. Validate. The build fails, naming the package, when:\n374\t   - the `license` field is missing;\n375\t   - any SPDX identifier in it (split on `(`, `)`, ` OR `, ` AND `,\n376\t     ` WITH `) is not in the allowlist `Apache-2.0`, `BSD-2-Clause`,\n377\t     `BSD-3-Clause`, `ISC`, `MIT`, `MPL-2.0`, `Unlicense` (the same list\n378\t     the Go CI passed to `go-licenses`);\n379\t   - no license file exists.\n380\t7. Render, sorted by `name` then `version`:\n381\t\n382\t```\n383\tThird-party software bundled in dist/cli.js\n384\t\n385\tRoast's npm package bundles the following packages. Each entry gives the\n386\tpackage, its declared license, and the license text it ships.\n387\t\n388\t==============================================================================\n389\t<name>@<version>\n390\tLicense: <license field>\n391\tRepository: <url>        (line omitted when the package has none)\n392\t\n393\t<contents of each license file, trimmed, separated by one blank line>\n394\t\n395\t==============================================================================\n396\t<next package> ...\n397\t```\n398\t\n399\tThe file ends with one newline. Output is deterministic for the same\n400\t`node_modules`.\n401\t\n402\t### 2.7 Schema generation hook (`scripts/schema.ts`)\n403\t\n404\tThe config area owns the zod schema and a pure function\n405\t`renderProjectSchema():string` in `src/config/json-schema.ts` that returns\n406\tthe full `roast.schema.json` text (`JSON.stringify(value, null, 2)` plus a\n407\ttrailing newline). This area owns the hook:\n408\t\n409\t1. `scripts/schema.ts` bundles `src/config/json-schema.ts` with the same\n410\t   base options as 2.5 (minus banner, defines, and metafile) into\n411\t   `node_modules/.cache/roast/schema.mjs`, dynamically imports it, and\n412\t   calls `renderProjectSchema()`.\n413\t2. It writes `roast.schema.json` at the repo root only when the content\n414\t   differs, and prints whether it changed.\n415\t3. `npm run build` runs it first, so a developer who edits the zod schema\n416\t   gets the committed file regenerated and sees it in `git status`.\n417\t4. CI runs `git diff --exit-code -- roast.schema.json` after the build, so\n418\t   a pull request that changed the schema without committing the\n419\t   regenerated file fails.\n420\t5. The config area's drift test (generated text equals the committed file)\n421\t   runs in the test bundle and catches drift when `test:run` is used\n422\t   without a build.\n423\t\n424\tThe hook lands in M1, when the config area's zod schema exists. In M0\n425\t`build` does not call it. During M1 to M5 the generated file must still\n426\tsatisfy the Go `TestSchemaMatchesConfigStruct`, which compares structure\n427\tand JSON types only, not formatting.\n428\t\n429\t### 2.8 Build info (`src/buildinfo.ts`)\n430\t\n431\tReplaces Go `internal/buildinfo`. Values come from the esbuild `define`s\n432\t(2.5). When a define is absent (the test bundle, the schema bundle), the\n433\tvalue is the sentinel: version `dev`, commit `unknown`, date `unknown`.\n434\tThe Go fallback to toolchain-embedded VCS data has no TS equivalent and is\n435\tdropped.\n436\t\n437\tFormat of the one-line string (Go `buildinfo.String`):\n438\t\n439\t- version is `dev` or date is `unknown`: `<version> (commit <commit>)`,\n440\t  for example `dev (commit unknown)`;\n441\t- otherwise `<version> (<commit>, <date>)`, for example\n442\t  `2.0.0 (abc1234, 2026-12-01T10:00:00Z)`.\n443\t\n444\tThe bundle's version, commit, and date are injected by esbuild `define`\n445\t(2.5); running from source (no define) reports `dev`.\n446\t\n447\tConsumers (owned by other areas): `--version` output, the `User-Agent`\n448\t`roast/<version>`, `roast doctor`'s `build` check (warn when version is\n449\t`dev`), and the run record's `roast.version` / `roast.commit`.\n450\t\n451\t### 2.9 Test runner pipeline\n452\t\n453\t1. `test/index.ts` imports every test module (`test/<area>/*.ts`); it is\n454\t   the only test entry. Tests use `@substrate-system/tapzero` (`test`,\n455\t   `t.ok`, `t.equal`, `t.deepEqual`, async tests).\n456\t2. `npm run build:test` runs `scripts/bundle.ts --test`: the 2.5 options\n457\t   with `entryPoints: ['test/index.ts']`, `outfile: 'test/test-bundle.js'`,\n458\t   `tsconfig: 'tsconfig.json'`, no shebang line in the banner (the\n459\t   `require` shim stays), no defines, no metafile.\n460\t3. `npm run test:tap` runs `node test/test-bundle.js` piped to `tap-spec`\n461\t   under `bash -o pipefail`, so the script fails when the bundle exits\n462\t   non-zero (a failed assertion, an uncaught error, a crash before the\n463\t   plan) even if the formatter exits 0. Bash is available on both\n464\t   supported platforms.\n465\t4. `npm test` builds the real bundle first, because the bundle smoke tests\n466\t   (5.1) spawn `dist/cli.js`.\n467\t5. Tests find the repo root from the bundle location:\n468\t   `new URL('..', import.meta.url)` (the bundle lives in `test/`).\n469\t6. Opt-in live provider tests (`ROAST_LIVE_*`) live under `test/live/`\n470\t   with their own entry `test/live/index.ts`, bundled to\n471\t   `test/live-bundle.js` by `scripts/bundle.ts --live` and run by\n472\t   `npm run test:live`. `test/index.ts` never imports them, so `npm test`\n473\t   cannot reach the network even with the variables set. CI never runs\n474\t   `test:live`.\n475\t7. Test hygiene that the tooling assumes: tests create temporary Git\n476\t   repositories with `GIT_AUTHOR_*`/`GIT_COMMITTER_*` set in the child\n477\t   environment (CI runners have no Git identity), isolate `HOME` and\n478\t   `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, and compare directories after `realpath` (macOS\n479\t   temp dirs are `/var/...` while Git prints `/private/var/...`).\n480\t\n481\tThe Go-specific notes go away: there is no race detector, so CI sets no\n482\t`GOFLAGS`; the rule that a `go` subprocess under `-race` must not set\n483\t`CGO_ENABLED=0` has no TS successor; `go mod tidy`, `gofmt`, `go vet`, and\n484\tstaticcheck U1000 are replaced by `tsc` (unused locals surface through the\n485\t`@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` lint rule). The only Go build left\n486\tafter M0 is the differential harness's baseline binary (2.13), which it\n487\tbuilds with `GOFLAGS` removed from the environment.\n488\t\n489\t### 2.10 Package check (`scripts/check-pack.ts`, slimmed)\n490\t\n491\tRun as `npm run check:pack` after `npm run build`, in CI and in\n492\t`prepublishOnly`. Operates on `process.cwd()` so tests can run it in a\n493\tfixture. Steps:\n494\t\n495\t1. `npm pack --dry-run --json` in the package root (no `--workspaces`).\n496\t   Non-zero exit: print npm's stderr, fail.\n497\t2. Parse stdout: npm 12 prints an object keyed by package name, older npm\n498\t   an array; accept both and take the single result's `files[].path`.\n499\t3. Fail unless the tarball lists each of `dist/cli.js`,\n500\t   `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`, `roast.schema.json`, `LICENSE.txt`,\n501\t   `LICENSE-MIT.txt`, `LICENSE-APACHE.txt`.\n502\t4. Fail when `package.json` declares no `license`, or declares a non-empty\n503\t   `dependencies` or any `optionalDependencies`.\n504\t5. Fail when `dist/cli.js` on disk does not start with\n505\t   `#!/usr/bin/env node\\n` or is not executable by its owner.\n506\t6. On failure print every problem (one per line, prefixed by\n507\t   `packaging check failed:`), then the hint to run `npm run build` and\n508\t   check `files`, and exit 1. On success print one summary line, exit 0.\n509\t\n510\t### 2.11 Release lifecycle\n511\t\n512\tPublishing is local only (no CI publish job), as at the baseline. The\n513\ttemplate's npm lifecycle replaces `scripts/release.ts`, `version.ts`,\n514\t`check-release.ts`, `platforms.ts`, and `licenses.sh`:\n515\t\n516\t```\n517\tnpm version <major|minor|patch|x.y.z>\n518\t  preversion      npm run lint\n519\t  (npm writes the version into package.json)\n520\t  version         README toc, CHANGELOG.md via auto-changelog, git add\n521\t  (npm commits and tags v<x.y.z>)\n522\t  postversion     git push --follow-tags && npm publish\n523\t    prepublishOnly  npm run build && npm run check:pack\n524\t```\n525\t\n526\tThe first TS release is `npm version 2.0.0` (explicit, because the\n527\tcommitted version is `0.0.0`). `publishConfig.access: public` replaces the\n528\t`--access public` flag that `scripts/release.ts` passed. A failing\n529\t`prepublishOnly` stops `npm publish` after the tag was pushed; the fix is\n530\ta follow-up patch release, not re-tagging.\n531\t\n532\tThe baseline invariants that existed only for platform packages (every\n533\tplatform version equals the root version, root `optionalDependencies` pin\n534\teach platform package, each platform `dist/` holds a binary and notices,\n535\tplatform packages publish before the root) disappear with the packages.\n536\t\n537\t### 2.12 CI workflows\n538\t\n539\t`claude-mention.yml`, `claude-review.yml`, and `pr-title.yml` are\n540\tunchanged. `ci.yml` (final form, after M6):\n541\t\n542\t- Triggers, top-level `permissions: {}`, and `concurrency` stay as at the\n543\t  baseline. Action references stay pinned by SHA as at the baseline\n544\t  (`actions/checkout` v7.0.1, `actions/setup-node` v7.1.0).\n545\t- Job `test`, `strategy.fail-fast: false`, matrix `os: [ubuntu-26.04,\n546\t  macos-latest]` (`macos-latest` is deliberately unpinned) by\n547\t  `node: [22, 24]`, `permissions: contents: read`,\n548\t  `timeout-minutes: 30`. Steps:\n549\t  1. Checkout (`persist-credentials: false`).\n550\t  2. Set up Node `${{ matrix.node }}`.\n551\t  3. Install: `npm install --package-lock-only --package-lock=true\n552\t     --no-audit --no-fund`, then `npm ci --no-audit --no-fund` (unchanged\n553\t     from the baseline; `npm ci` needs a lockfile and none is committed).\n554\t  4. `npm run lint`.\n555\t  5. `npm run typecheck`.\n556\t  6. `npm test` (builds, then runs the test bundle).\n557\t  7. `git diff --exit-code -- roast.schema.json`.\n558\t  8. `npm run check:pack`.\n559\t- Job `security` (ubuntu only): keeps the Git-history secret scan\n560\t  (gitleaks through `.github/tools/gitleaks/go.mod`) and workflow lint"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"453ecfdf-dc0d-4287-be41-1cc75a67a074","uuid":"b32560f7-e57b-41fb-ac6f-d88c9a444441","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:02:41.536Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-01-m0-scaffold/.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/15-packaging.md","content":"# Area 15: packaging, build, tooling, release, cutover\n\n## 1. Purpose\n\nThis area defines how Roast is built, tested, linted, checked, released, and\nshipped as one pure-JS npm package, `@substrate-system/roast`. It replaces\nthe Go toolchain, the six platform packages, the npm launcher, and the\nplatform release scripts. It also defines two milestones: the M0 scaffold\n(tooling that lets the other areas land code and tests) and the M6 cutover\n(deleting the Go implementation and releasing `2.0.0`).\n\nVocabulary: \"the bundle\" is `dist/cli.js`, the single esbuild ESM output\nthat `bin.roast` points at. \"Third-party notices\" is\n`dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`. \"The test bundle\" is\n`test/test-bundle.js`, the esbuild output of `test/index.ts`. \"The\nbaseline\" is Go commit `cd08f10`.\n\nUsers install Roast as a project dependency\n(`npm i -D @substrate-system/roast`) and run it as `npx roast ...`; it is\nnever a `PATH` binary. Installing it adds no transitive packages.\n\n## 2. Behavior contract\n\nThis section is the build and release contract, not CLI behavior.\n\n### 2.1 Package manifest (final form, after M6)\n\n`package.json` at the repo root, exactly these keys (key order is not\nsignificant; values are):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"@substrate-system/roast\",\n  \"version\": \"2.0.0\",\n  \"description\": \"Adversarial review\",\n  \"license\": \"(MIT OR Apache-2.0)\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"bin\": {\n    \"roast\": \"dist/cli.js\"\n  },\n  \"files\": [\n    \"dist/cli.js\",\n    \"dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt\",\n    \"roast.schema.json\",\n    \"LICENSE.txt\",\n    \"LICENSE-MIT.txt\",\n    \"LICENSE-APACHE.txt\"\n  ],\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=22.18\"\n  },\n  \"os\": [\"darwin\", \"linux\"],\n  \"publishConfig\": {\n    \"access\": \"public\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"lint\": \"eslint src test scripts eslint.config.js\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc -p tsconfig.json\",\n    \"schema\": \"node scripts/schema.ts\",\n    \"build\": \"npm run schema && node scripts/bundle.ts\",\n    \"build:test\": \"node scripts/bundle.ts --test\",\n    \"test\": \"npm run build && npm run test:run\",\n    \"test:run\": \"npm run build:test && npm run test:tap\",\n    \"test:tap\": \"bash -o pipefail -c 'node test/test-bundle.js | tap-spec'\",\n    \"test:live\": \"node scripts/bundle.ts --live && node test/live-bundle.js\",\n    \"check:pack\": \"node scripts/check-pack.ts\",\n    \"toc\": \"markdown-toc --maxdepth 3 -i README.md\",\n    \"preversion\": \"npm run lint\",\n    \"version\": \"npm run toc && auto-changelog && npm run stage:docs\",\n    \"stage:docs\": \"git add CHANGELOG.md README.md\",\n    \"postversion\": \"git push --follow-tags && npm publish\",\n    \"prepublishOnly\": \"npm run build && npm run check:pack\"\n  },\n  \"auto-changelog\": {\n    \"package\": true,\n    \"template\": \"keepachangelog\",\n    \"breakingPattern\": \"BREAKING CHANGE:\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@substrate-system/debug\": \"^0.9.64\",\n    \"@substrate-system/redeye\": \"^0.1.7\",\n    \"@substrate-system/tapzero\": \"^0.10.15\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"^22.18.0\",\n    \"@types/yargs\": \"^17.0.33\",\n    \"auto-changelog\": \"^2.4.0\",\n    \"esbuild\": \"^0.27.0\",\n    \"eslint\": \"^10.6.0\",\n    \"jsonc-parser\": \"^3.3.1\",\n    \"markdown-toc\": \"^1.2.0\",\n    \"newneostandard\": \"^0.14.1\",\n    \"tap-spec\": \"^5.0.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^7.0.2\",\n    \"typescript-eslint\": \"^8.62.0\",\n    \"yargs\": \"^18.2.0\",\n    \"zod\": \"^4.6.7\"\n  },\n  \"keywords\": [\"AI\"],\n  \"homepage\": \"https://github.com/nichoth/roast#readme\",\n  \"bugs\": { \"url\": \"https://github.com/nichoth/roast/issues\" },\n  \"repository\": {\n    \"type\": \"git\",\n    \"url\": \"git+https://github.com/nichoth/roast.git\"\n  },\n  \"author\": \"nichoth\"\n}\n```\n\nRules the manifest must keep:\n\n1. No `dependencies`, `optionalDependencies`, `peerDependencies`, or\n   `workspaces`. The runtime libraries (`yargs`, `zod`, `jsonc-parser`,\n   `@substrate-system/debug`) are `devDependencies` and bundled into\n   `dist/cli.js`. Anything in `dependencies` would install into every\n   user's project. (The working tree at the time of writing moved\n   `jsonc-parser`, `yargs`, `zod` into `dependencies`; that is wrong for\n   the TS package and must be reverted to `devDependencies`.)\n2. No `main` or `exports`. Roast is CLI only; importing the package fails.\n3. `files` lists exact paths, so `dist/meta.json` (the esbuild metafile)\n   and any other build by-product never ship.\n4. `roast.schema.json` stays at the package root. `roast init` writes a\n   `$schema` of `node_modules/@substrate-system/roast/roast.schema.json`\n   (see the init area), so the package name and this path are a contract.\n5. `os` makes npm refuse the install on Windows (EBADPLATFORM).\n6. `engines.node` `>=22.18` is the floor because Node 22.18 runs `.ts`\n   files with type stripping unflagged (the `scripts/*.ts` tooling relies\n   on it) and `node:zlib` has zstd from 22.15.\n7. `devEngines` (present at the baseline) is removed: `engines` now states\n   the same floor.\n8. `@types/node` tracks the engine floor's major (22), so code cannot\n   typecheck against an API newer than the minimum supported Node.\n9. `version` is `2.0.0` only after the M6 release; during M0 to M5 it stays\n   whatever the baseline has (`0.0.0`).\n\nThe `auto-changelog` options live in the `\"auto-changelog\"` key\n(auto-changelog reads it from `package.json`) and the `git add` is split\ninto `stage:docs`, so every script fits in 80 columns.\n\n`CHANGELOG.md` keeps its existing history (the upstream 1.4.x entries\nstay as committed). From `2.0.0` on, `auto-changelog` regenerates the\nnew entries from git tags at each `npm version`.\n\n`@types/yargs` is a `devDependency` because yargs 18 does not ship its\nown types.\n\n### 2.2 npm config and ignores\n\n`.npmrc` (final form) is the template's single line:\n\n```\npackage-lock=false\n```\n\nThe baseline's `force=true` existed only so npm would link the\n`os`/`cpu`-restricted workspaces; it is removed at M6 together with\n`packages/`. There is still no committed lockfile.\n\n`.gitignore` gains `test/*.js` (the test bundles). At M6 it drops the\nGo-era entries `/bin/`, `/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/`, `*.test`, `/roast`,\n`/roast.exe`. `dist/` stays ignored.\n\nNo `.npmignore`: the `files` allowlist governs the tarball.\n\n### 2.3 TypeScript config\n\n`tsconfig.json` (typecheck only; esbuild does all emitting):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"module\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"Bundler\",\n    \"lib\": [\"ES2022\"],\n    \"types\": [\"node\"],\n    \"allowJs\": false,\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"forceConsistentCasingInFileNames\": true,\n    \"resolveJsonModule\": true,\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"src\", \"test\", \"scripts\"]\n}\n```\n\n`tsconfig.build.json` (passed to esbuild as `tsconfig` for the bundle):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.json\",\n  \"exclude\": [\"test\", \"scripts\"]\n}\n```\n\nDifferences from `../template-ts-browser/tsconfig.json` and why:\n\n- `lib` has no `DOM` or `WebWorker`; `types` is `[\"node\"]`, not\n  `vite/client`. `fetch`, `AbortSignal`, `TextDecoder`, and\n  `ReadableStream` come from `@types/node`.\n- `noImplicitAny: false` is dropped, so `strict` is fully on.\n- `experimentalDecorators`, `emitDecoratorMetadata`, `declaration*`,\n  `sourceMap`, `outDir`, `listFiles` are dropped: no decorators, no\n  library output, no tsc emit.\n- `allowImportingTsExtensions` plus `noEmit`: `scripts/*.ts` run directly\n  under Node type stripping, which requires `.ts` in relative imports.\n  Code under `src/` and `test/` imports siblings with the `.js` extension\n  (template style); `Bundler` resolution maps it to the `.ts` file.\n- `include` drops `example` and `lib.es5.d.ts`, adds `scripts`.\n\nNode-run scripts (`scripts/*.ts`) may use only erasable TypeScript syntax:\nno `enum`, `namespace`, parameter properties, or decorators. Type-only\nimports must use `import type`.\n\nAmbient declarations in `src/assets.d.ts`:\n\n```ts\ndeclare module '*.tmpl' {\n    const text:string\n    export default text\n}\ndeclare module '*.md' {\n    const text:string\n    export default text\n}\ndeclare module '*.sh' {\n    const text:string\n    export default text\n}\ndeclare const __ROAST_VERSION__:string|undefined\ndeclare const __ROAST_COMMIT__:string|undefined\ndeclare const __ROAST_DATE__:string|undefined\n```\n\n### 2.4 Lint\n\n`eslint.config.js` is copied from `../template-ts-browser/eslint.config.js`\nbyte for byte: the `newneostandard({ ts: true })` base, the Standard Style\noverrides, the `@typescript-eslint/recommended` block, and the local\n`union-spacing` rule. Its rules are not changed. Its `ignores` array is\nkept as is (`lib.es5.d.ts`, `dist/**`, `public/**`, `test/*.js`); the\nentries that do not match anything in Roast are harmless.\n\nThe `lint` script names directories (`src test scripts eslint.config.js`)\ninstead of the template's `./**/*.{ts,js}`, because flat-config eslint\ndoes not skip dot-directories such as `.scratch/` and `.claude/`.\n\nConsequences the code must respect (from those rules): 4-space indent, no\nsemicolons, single quotes, `name:Type` with no spaces around the colon,\nobject literal members as `{ a:1 }` (`key-spacing` with `afterColon:\nfalse`), `A|B` unions with no spaces, `import type` for type-only imports,\nunused variables only with a `_` prefix.\n\nDuring M0 to M5 the legacy files do not follow these rules (they use\n`{ cwd: ROOT }` spacing). The transitional `lint` script adds\n`--ignore-pattern` flags for them instead of editing the config; see 2.14.\n\n### 2.5 The bundle (`scripts/bundle.ts`)\n\n`npm run build` runs `npm run schema` (2.7), then `node scripts/bundle.ts`,\nwhich:\n\n1. Removes and recreates `dist/`.\n2. Calls `esbuild.build` with the options below.\n3. Writes the metafile to `dist/meta.json`.\n4. Writes `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt` from the metafile (2.6).\n5. `chmod 0o755 dist/cli.js`. npm sets the bin mode on install, but links\n   it does not refresh (an existing npx cache entry, `npx roast` inside\n   this repo) need the file executable already.\n6. Exits non-zero on any esbuild error or notice-generation error. Esbuild\n   warnings are printed and do not fail the build.\n\nEsbuild options for the bundle:\n\n```ts\nconst options:BuildOptions = {\n    entryPoints: ['src/cli.ts'],\n    outfile: 'dist/cli.js',\n    bundle: true,\n    platform: 'node',\n    format: 'esm',\n    target: 'node22',\n    tsconfig: 'tsconfig.build.json',\n    mainFields: ['module', 'main'],\n    keepNames: true,\n    minify: false,\n    sourcemap: false,\n    metafile: true,\n    loader: { '.tmpl': 'text', '.md': 'text', '.sh': 'text' },\n    banner: { js: BANNER },\n    define: {\n        __ROAST_VERSION__: JSON.stringify(version),\n        __ROAST_COMMIT__: JSON.stringify(commit),\n        __ROAST_DATE__: JSON.stringify(date),\n    },\n    logLevel: 'warning',\n}\n```\n\nWhere:\n\n- `BANNER` is three lines: `#!/usr/bin/env node`, then\n  `import { createRequire as __roastRequire } from 'node:module'`, then\n  `const require = __roastRequire(import.meta.url)`. The shebang must be\n  the first line of the file. The `require` shim exists because esbuild's\n  ESM output turns a bundled CommonJS module's `require('node:fs')` into a\n  runtime \"Dynamic require is not supported\" error unless a `require` is\n  in scope.\n- `mainFields: ['module', 'main']` overrides esbuild's Node default\n  (`main` first). `jsonc-parser`'s `main` is a UMD build whose internal\n  `require` calls esbuild cannot follow; its `module` field is the ESM\n  build.\n- `version` is the root `package.json` `version`. `commit` is\n  `git rev-parse --short=7 HEAD` and `date` is `git log -1 --format=%cI`\n  (committer date, RFC 3339), both run at the repo root. If either `git`\n  call fails (a build from a tarball), the value is `unknown`. These are\n  the same three values the Go build stamped through `-ldflags -X`.\n- `minify: false` and `keepNames: true` keep user-reported stack traces\n  readable. `legalComments` keeps esbuild's bundle default (`eof`).\n\nThe yargs locale caveat. yargs loads translations with `y18n` from a\n`locales/` directory next to its own module file. In the bundle that\ndirectory does not exist. y18n treats a missing locale file as an empty\ntable and returns the English source strings, so help and error text stay\nEnglish. The CLI must still call `.locale('en')` and `.detectLocale(false)`\nso yargs never tries to read `LANG`/`LC_ALL` and no locale file is ever\nprobed. A bundle smoke test (5.1) proves output is identical under a\nnon-English locale. If a future yargs version throws on the missing\ndirectory, the fix is in the bundle step (copy nothing; pass an explicit\n`y18n` instance or stub), never shipping `locales/`.\n\nText assets. Prompt templates, the agent skill `SKILL.md`, and the\npre-commit hook script are imported as strings through the text loader\n(`import finderCore from './templates/finder_core.tmpl'`). The string must\nequal the file's bytes decoded as UTF-8; none of these files has a BOM.\nLocation of the files:\n\n- prompt templates (the 12 `*.tmpl` files): `internal/prompts/templates/`\n  during M1 to M5, `src/prompts/templates/` after M6;\n- agent skill: `internal/skill/assets/roast/SKILL.md`, then\n  `src/skill/assets/roast/SKILL.md`;\n- hook script: `internal/gate/pre-commit.sh`, then\n  `src/gate/pre-commit.sh`.\n\nUntil M6 the TS modules import the assets from their Go locations, so the\nGo `//go:embed` directives and the TS bundle read the same file and cannot\ndrift. M6 moves them with `git mv` and updates the import paths. Go embeds\n`all:assets/roast` as a directory; the TS skill module imports each file\nexplicitly, so a new file under `assets/roast/` needs a new import.\n\n`npx roast` inside this repository resolves the root package's own `bin`.\nBuild first: with no `dist/cli.js`, a `roast` elsewhere on `PATH` (for\nexample Homebrew) can answer instead.\n\n### 2.6 Third-party notices (`scripts/licenses.ts`)\n\nGenerated by the bundle step from the in-memory metafile. Algorithm:\n\n1. Take `metafile.outputs['dist/cli.js'].inputs`. Keep only input paths\n   with `bytesInOutput > 0` (code actually in the bundle) that contain a\n   `node_modules/` segment.\n2. For each path, the package root is the prefix up to and including the\n   package name after the last `node_modules/`: one segment, or two when\n   the first starts with `@` (scoped). Nested `node_modules` resolve to\n   the innermost package.\n3. Read `<root>/package.json`: `name`, `version`, `license` (a string; the\n   legacy object or array `licenses` form is an error), and `repository`\n   (string or `{ url }`, optional).\n4. License files are the files directly in `<root>` whose name matches\n   `/^(licen[cs]e|copying|notice)(\\..*)?$/i`, sorted by name.\n5. Deduplicate by `name@version`.\n6. Validate. The build fails, naming the package, when:\n   - the `license` field is missing;\n   - any SPDX identifier in it (split on `(`, `)`, ` OR `, ` AND `,\n     ` WITH `) is not in the allowlist `Apache-2.0`, `BSD-2-Clause`,\n     `BSD-3-Clause`, `ISC`, `MIT`, `MPL-2.0`, `Unlicense` (the same list\n     the Go CI passed to `go-licenses`);\n   - no license file exists.\n7. Render, sorted by `name` then `version`:\n\n```\nThird-party software bundled in dist/cli.js\n\nRoast's npm package bundles the following packages. Each entry gives the\npackage, its declared license, and the license text it ships.\n\n==============================================================================\n<name>@<version>\nLicense: <license field>\nRepository: <url>        (line omitted when the package has none)\n\n<contents of each license file, trimmed, separated by one blank line>\n\n==============================================================================\n<next package> ...\n```\n\nThe file ends with one newline. Output is deterministic for the same\n`node_modules`.\n\n### 2.7 Schema generation hook (`scripts/schema.ts`)\n\nThe config area owns the zod schema and a pure function\n`renderProjectSchema():string` in `src/config/json-schema.ts` that returns\nthe full `roast.schema.json` text (`JSON.stringify(value, null, 2)` plus a\ntrailing newline). This area owns the hook:\n\n1. `scripts/schema.ts` bundles `src/config/json-schema.ts` with the same\n   base options as 2.5 (minus banner, defines, and metafile) into\n   `node_modules/.cache/roast/schema.mjs`, dynamically imports it, and\n   calls `renderProjectSchema()`.\n2. It writes `roast.schema.json` at the repo root only when the content\n   differs, and prints whether it changed.\n3. `npm run build` runs it first, so a developer who edits the zod schema\n   gets the committed file regenerated and sees it in `git status`.\n4. CI runs `git diff --exit-code -- roast.schema.json` after the build, so\n   a pull request that changed the schema without committing the\n   regenerated file fails.\n5. The config area's drift test (generated text equals the committed file)\n   runs in the test bundle and catches drift when `test:run` is used\n   without a build.\n\nThe hook lands in M1, when the config area's zod schema exists. In M0\n`build` does not call it. During M1 to M5 the generated file must still\nsatisfy the Go `TestSchemaMatchesConfigStruct`, which compares structure\nand JSON types only, not formatting.\n\n### 2.8 Build info (`src/buildinfo.ts`)\n\nReplaces Go `internal/buildinfo`. Values come from the esbuild `define`s\n(2.5). When a define is absent (the test bundle, the schema bundle), the\nvalue is the sentinel: version `dev`, commit `unknown`, date `unknown`.\nThe Go fallback to toolchain-embedded VCS data has no TS equivalent and is\ndropped.\n\nFormat of the one-line string (Go `buildinfo.String`):\n\n- version is `dev` or date is `unknown`: `<version> (commit <commit>)`,\n  for example `dev (commit unknown)`;\n- otherwise `<version> (<commit>, <date>)`, for example\n  `2.0.0 (abc1234, 2026-12-01T10:00:00Z)`.\n\nThe bundle's version, commit, and date are injected by esbuild `define`\n(2.5); running from source (no define) reports `dev`.\n\nConsumers (owned by other areas): `--version` output, the `User-Agent`\n`roast/<version>`, `roast doctor`'s `build` check (warn when version is\n`dev`), and the run record's `roast.version` / `roast.commit`.\n\n### 2.9 Test runner pipeline\n\n1. `test/index.ts` imports every test module (`test/<area>/*.ts`); it is\n   the only test entry. Tests use `@substrate-system/tapzero` (`test`,\n   `t.ok`, `t.equal`, `t.deepEqual`, async tests).\n2. `npm run build:test` runs `scripts/bundle.ts --test`: the 2.5 options\n   with `entryPoints: ['test/index.ts']`, `outfile: 'test/test-bundle.js'`,\n   `tsconfig: 'tsconfig.json'`, no shebang line in the banner (the\n   `require` shim stays), no defines, no metafile.\n3. `npm run test:tap` runs `node test/test-bundle.js` piped to `tap-spec`\n   under `bash -o pipefail`, so the script fails when the bundle exits\n   non-zero (a failed assertion, an uncaught error, a crash before the\n   plan) even if the formatter exits 0. Bash is available on both\n   supported platforms.\n4. `npm test` builds the real bundle first, because the bundle smoke tests\n   (5.1) spawn `dist/cli.js`.\n5. Tests find the repo root from the bundle location:\n   `new URL('..', import.meta.url)` (the bundle lives in `test/`).\n6. Opt-in live provider tests (`ROAST_LIVE_*`) live under `test/live/`\n   with their own entry `test/live/index.ts`, bundled to\n   `test/live-bundle.js` by `scripts/bundle.ts --live` and run by\n   `npm run test:live`. `test/index.ts` never imports them, so `npm test`\n   cannot reach the network even with the variables set. CI never runs\n   `test:live`.\n7. Test hygiene that the tooling assumes: tests create temporary Git\n   repositories with `GIT_AUTHOR_*`/`GIT_COMMITTER_*` set in the child\n   environment (CI runners have no Git identity), isolate `HOME` and\n   `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, and compare directories after `realpath` (macOS\n   temp dirs are `/var/...` while Git prints `/private/var/...`).\n\nThe Go-specific notes go away: there is no race detector, so CI sets no\n`GOFLAGS`; the rule that a `go` subprocess under `-race` must not set\n`CGO_ENABLED=0` has no TS successor; `go mod tidy`, `gofmt`, `go vet`, and\nstaticcheck U1000 are replaced by `tsc` (unused locals surface through the\n`@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` lint rule). The only Go build left\nafter M0 is the differential harness's baseline binary (2.13), which it\nbuilds with `GOFLAGS` removed from the environment.\n\n### 2.10 Package check (`scripts/check-pack.ts`, slimmed)\n\nRun as `npm run check:pack` after `npm run build`, in CI and in\n`prepublishOnly`. Operates on `process.cwd()` so tests can run it in a\nfixture. Steps:\n\n1. `npm pack --dry-run --json` in the package root (no `--workspaces`).\n   Non-zero exit: print npm's stderr, fail.\n2. Parse stdout: npm 12 prints an object keyed by package name, older npm\n   an array; accept both and take the single result's `files[].path`.\n3. Fail unless the tarball lists each of `dist/cli.js`,\n   `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`, `roast.schema.json`, `LICENSE.txt`,\n   `LICENSE-MIT.txt`, `LICENSE-APACHE.txt`.\n4. Fail when `package.json` declares no `license`, or declares a non-empty\n   `dependencies` or any `optionalDependencies`.\n5. Fail when `dist/cli.js` on disk does not start with\n   `#!/usr/bin/env node\\n` or is not executable by its owner.\n6. On failure print every problem (one per line, prefixed by\n   `packaging check failed:`), then the hint to run `npm run build` and\n   check `files`, and exit 1. On success print one summary line, exit 0.\n\n### 2.11 Release lifecycle\n\nPublishing is local only (no CI publish job), as at the baseline. The\ntemplate's npm lifecycle replaces `scripts/release.ts`, `version.ts`,\n`check-release.ts`, `platforms.ts`, and `licenses.sh`:\n\n```\nnpm version <major|minor|patch|x.y.z>\n  preversion      npm run lint\n  (npm writes the version into package.json)\n  version         README toc, CHANGELOG.md via auto-changelog, git add\n  (npm commits and tags v<x.y.z>)\n  postversion     git push --follow-tags && npm publish\n    prepublishOnly  npm run build && npm run check:pack\n```\n\nThe first TS release is `npm version 2.0.0` (explicit, because the\ncommitted version is `0.0.0`). `publishConfig.access: public` replaces the\n`--access public` flag that `scripts/release.ts` passed. A failing\n`prepublishOnly` stops `npm publish` after the tag was pushed; the fix is\na follow-up patch release, not re-tagging.\n\nThe baseline invariants that existed only for platform packages (every\nplatform version equals the root version, root `optionalDependencies` pin\neach platform package, each platform `dist/` holds a binary and notices,\nplatform packages publish before the root) disappear with the packages.\n\n### 2.12 CI workflows\n\n`claude-mention.yml`, `claude-review.yml`, and `pr-title.yml` are\nunchanged. `ci.yml` (final form, after M6):\n\n- Triggers, top-level `permissions: {}`, and `concurrency` stay as at the\n  baseline. Action references stay pinned by SHA as at the baseline\n  (`actions/checkout` v7.0.1, `actions/setup-node` v7.1.0).\n- Job `test`, `strategy.fail-fast: false`, matrix `os: [ubuntu-26.04,\n  macos-latest]` (`macos-latest` is deliberately unpinned) by\n  `node: [22, 24]`, `permissions: contents: read`,\n  `timeout-minutes: 30`. Steps:\n  1. Checkout (`persist-credentials: false`).\n  2. Set up Node `${{ matrix.node }}`.\n  3. Install: `npm install --package-lock-only --package-lock=true\n     --no-audit --no-fund`, then `npm ci --no-audit --no-fund` (unchanged\n     from the baseline; `npm ci` needs a lockfile and none is committed).\n  4. `npm run lint`.\n  5. `npm run typecheck`.\n  6. `npm test` (builds, then runs the test bundle).\n  7. `git diff --exit-code -- roast.schema.json`.\n  8. `npm run check:pack`.\n- Job `security` (ubuntu only): keeps the Git-history secret scan\n  (gitleaks through `.github/tools/gitleaks/go.mod`) and workflow lint","numLines":560,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1036}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018fRp4YMdJsJHZxCdWo3Ujd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
