{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018Bj7FMoWDHKwV6BC3PP6xy","type":"tool_result","content":"560\t  (gitleaks through `.github/tools/gitleaks/go.mod`) and workflow lint\n561\t  (actionlint through `.github/tools/actionlint/go.mod`). It adds two\n562\t  steps: `npm audit --audit-level=high`, run after the install step\n563\t  (without `--omit=dev`, so the bundled runtime libraries, which are\n564\t  `devDependencies`, are covered), and `shellcheck\n565\t  src/gate/pre-commit.sh` (the hook script is the only shell file left).\n566\t  `setup-go` stays\n567\t  only for these tool modules, with `go-version-file` pointing at the\n568\t  tool's own `go.mod` and `cache-dependency-path: .github/tools/*/go.sum`.\n569\t  The tool modules' `go mod tidy` check stays, limited to `.github/tools`.\n570\t\n571\tBaseline steps removed at M6: Set up Go in the test job, `go mod\n572\tdownload`, gofmt check, root `go mod tidy` check, `shellcheck\n573\tscripts/*.sh` (replaced by the hook-script step above), `GOFLAGS: -race`\n574\ton Test, `go vet`,\n575\tstaticcheck, \"Build all platform packages\", govulncheck, `go-licenses\n576\tcheck` (replaced by the allowlist in 2.6), and `bash scripts/licenses.sh`.\n577\tTool modules deleted with them: `.github/tools/staticcheck`,\n578\t`.github/tools/govulncheck`, `.github/tools/licenses`.\n579\t\n580\tDuring M0 to M5, `ci.yml` keeps every baseline job and adds the job\n581\t`typescript` (2.14) and the differential harness job (2.13).\n582\t\n583\t### 2.13 Go-vs-TS differential harness (temporary)\n584\t\n585\tPurpose: prove parity on observable output by running the baseline Go CLI\n586\tand the TS CLI on identical inputs against the same fake inference server.\n587\tIt lives in `test/diff/` with entry `test/diff/index.ts`, bundled to\n588\t`test/diff-bundle.js` by `scripts/bundle.ts --diff`, run by\n589\t`npm run test:diff`. It is not imported by `test/index.ts` and is deleted\n590\tat M6.\n591\t\n592\tCI runs it from M1 to M5 on Ubuntu only (a job in `ci.yml` with Go set\n593\tup, then `npm run build` and `npm run test:diff`), with an allowlist of\n594\tthe deliberate changes listed in spec.md, \"Deliberate changes from the Go\n595\tbaseline\". Differences outside the allowlist fail the job.\n596\t\n597\tBuilding the Go baseline:\n598\t\n599\t1. Binary cache path: `node_modules/.cache/roast-diff/roast-go-cd08f10`.\n600\t   Reuse it if present.\n601\t2. Otherwise: `git worktree add --detach <tmp>/roast-go cd08f10`, then in\n602\t   it `go build -trimpath -ldflags \"-X\n603\t   github.com/bluesky-social/roast/internal/buildinfo.Version=baseline\" -o\n604\t   <cache path> ./cmd/roast` with `CGO_ENABLED=0` and `GOFLAGS` removed\n605\t   from the environment, then `git worktree remove --force <tmp>/roast-go`\n606\t   (also on failure).\n607\t3. If `go` is not on `PATH`, the harness prints a TAP skip for every\n608\t   scenario and exits 0 (CI installs Go, so it never skips there).\n609\t\n610\tThe TS side is `dist/cli.js` (the harness requires `npm run build` first),\n611\tspawned as `node dist/cli.js`, not the in-process `run`, so both CLIs are\n612\texercised as processes.\n613\t\n614\tPer scenario:\n615\t\n616\t1. Start one `node:http` fake server (the same fake the CLI tests use,\n617\t   speaking the `chat`, `responses`, and `anthropic` protocols). Responses\n618\t   are scripted per scenario and selected by request content (model name\n619\t   plus number of conversation turns), never by arrival order, because\n620\t   finder and verifier calls may interleave differently.\n621\t2. Build two identical fixture repositories, one per CLI, from the same\n622\t   function: fixed file contents, fixed `GIT_AUTHOR_DATE` /\n623\t   `GIT_COMMITTER_DATE` and identity, so commit IDs match.\n624\t3. Write the same `.roast.json` (profiles on the fake's URL, credentials\n625\t   via `api_key_env`) into both. Each CLI approves its own copy with\n626\t   `trust --yes` first: trust hashes differ by design (v1 vs v2).\n627\t4. Run each CLI with a scrubbed environment: no `ROAST_*`, `OPENAI_*`,\n628\t   `OPENROUTER_*`, `ANTHROPIC_*`, `DEBUG`; private `HOME` and\n629\t   `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`; the profile's key variable set.\n630\t5. Compare, after normalization:\n631\t   - exit code (exact);\n632\t   - stdout when the scenario requests JSON output (parsed, deep equal);\n633\t   - requests the fake received, grouped by (model, turn count): method,\n634\t     path, parsed JSON body deep equal, and header names (values compared\n635\t     only for `Content-Type` and the auth scheme). This covers the\n636\t     rendered `finder_user` / `verifier_user` prompts, which reach the\n637\t     fake verbatim;\n638\t   - run records: the set of relative file paths in the run directory;\n639\t     every JSON and JSONL file parsed and deep equal; raw response\n640\t     captures byte equal; run bundles compared as decompressed tar entries\n641\t     (name, mode, size, content), not compressed bytes, because the zstd\n642\t     encoders differ.\n643\t   Normalization replaces run IDs, timestamps, durations, the fixture\n644\t   repository path, `roast.version` / `roast.commit`, the `User-Agent`\n645\t   value, and session header values with placeholders.\n646\t6. Not compared: stderr, rendered Markdown, help text, and anything\n647\t   touched by a deliberate change (trust messages and `trust.json`, the\n648\t   `completion` command, debug output).\n649\t\n650\tScenarios are added per milestone (M1: config errors and `gate settings`;\n651\tM3: clean review, review with findings, `--json`, `--staged`,\n652\t`--max-severity`, a failing provider; M4: the same review scenarios on\n653\t`responses` and `anthropic`; M5: `runs` listing and snapshot commands,\n654\t`init` with a fake provider). A scenario that fails because Go behavior\n655\twas judged wrong is recorded in the owning area's Open questions, not\n656\tpatched in the harness.\n657\t\n658\t### 2.14 M0 scaffold\n659\t\n660\tM0 lets the other areas land TS code and tests while the Go build, the\n661\tlauncher, and the platform release flow keep working unchanged. Contents:\n662\t\n663\t1. `package.json`: add the `devDependencies` from 2.1 (keeping the\n664\t   baseline ones, and moving `jsonc-parser`, `yargs`, `zod` out of\n665\t   `dependencies`); add scripts `lint`, `typecheck`, `bundle`\n666\t   (`node scripts/bundle.ts`), `build:test`, `test:tap`, `test:ts`\n667\t   (`npm run bundle && npm run build:test && npm run test:tap`),\n668\t   `test:diff` (`npm run bundle && node scripts/bundle.ts --diff &&\n669\t   node test/diff-bundle.js`). `build`, `build:launcher`, `test`, `version`,\n670\t   `prepublishOnly`, `check:pack`, `release` keep their baseline meaning.\n671\t   `bin`, `files`, `workspaces`, `engines`, `optionalDependencies` are\n672\t   untouched.\n673\t2. The transitional `lint` script:\n674\t   `eslint src test scripts eslint.config.js` plus one `--ignore-pattern`\n675\t   per legacy file: `src/launcher.ts`, `test/*.test.ts`,\n676\t   `test/release-fixture.ts`, `scripts/build.ts`, `scripts/check-pack.ts`,\n677\t   `scripts/check-release.ts`, `scripts/platforms.ts`,\n678\t   `scripts/release.ts`, `scripts/version.ts`.\n679\t3. TypeScript: `tsconfig.json` becomes 2.3's file plus `exclude` of the\n680\t   same legacy files; `tsconfig.build.json` as in 2.3. The launcher's\n681\t   current config moves to `tsconfig.launcher.json` and `build:launcher`\n682\t   becomes `tsc -p tsconfig.launcher.json`.\n683\t4. `eslint.config.js` copied from the template (2.4).\n684\t5. New tooling: `scripts/bundle.ts` (with `--test`, `--live`, `--diff`),\n685\t   `scripts/licenses.ts`. `scripts/schema.ts` lands in M1. The slimmed\n686\t   package check is written as `scripts/check-package.ts` (it would fail\n687\t   against the transitional manifest, so CI does not run it yet; its\n688\t   fixture tests do run); M6 renames it to `scripts/check-pack.ts` over\n689\t   the old one.\n690\t6. Source: `src/cli.ts` (the bundle entry; it only hands\n691\t   `process.argv.slice(2)` and the real process IO to the CLI area's\n692\t   `run` and sets `process.exitCode` from its result; in M0 `run` handles\n693\t   `--version` only), `src/buildinfo.ts`, `src/assets.d.ts`.\n694\t7. Tests: `test/index.ts` importing `test/tooling/*.ts` (5.1 to 5.4).\n695\t8. `.gitignore`: add `test/*.js`.\n696\t9. CI: new job `typescript` in `ci.yml` with the 2.12 matrix and steps\n697\t   checkout, setup-node, install, `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`,\n698\t   `npm run test:ts`. The baseline `quality` and `security` jobs are\n699\t   unchanged until M6.\n700\t10. `.npmrc` keeps `force=true` until M6 (the workspaces still exist).\n701\t11. License check: `@substrate-system/debug` and every dependency it\n702\t    pulls into the bundle must pass the 2.6 allowlist. M0 runs the\n703\t    bundle with the license step against them and resolves any failure\n704\t    (replace the library or extend the allowlist with maintainer\n705\t    approval) before other areas depend on it.\n706\t\n707\t### 2.15 M6 cutover checklist\n708\t\n709\tPreconditions: every area's test plan is ported and green; the\n710\tdifferential harness passes every scenario (or each difference is an\n711\taccepted Open question); `npm run build && npm run check:pack` passes\n712\tagainst the final manifest in a scratch commit.\n713\t\n714\t1. Move assets with `git mv` (list in 2.5) and update their imports.\n715\t2. Delete Go: `cmd/`, `internal/`, `go.mod`, `go.sum`.\n716\t3. Delete npm-packaging code: `packages/`, `src/launcher.ts`,\n717\t   `tsconfig.launcher.json`, `scripts/build.ts`, the old\n718\t   `scripts/check-pack.ts`, `scripts/check-release.ts`,\n719\t   `scripts/platforms.ts`, `scripts/release.ts`, `scripts/version.ts`,\n720\t   `scripts/licenses.sh`, `scripts/licenses_test.go`, and their tests\n721\t   `test/launcher.test.ts`, `test/manifest.test.ts`,\n722\t   `test/check-pack.test.ts`, `test/prepublish.test.ts`,\n723\t   `test/release.test.ts`, `test/version.test.ts`,\n724\t   `test/release-fixture.ts`.\n725\t4. Rename `scripts/check-package.ts` to `scripts/check-pack.ts`.\n726\t5. Delete the differential harness: `test/diff/`, the `--diff` mode of\n727\t   `scripts/bundle.ts`, the `test:diff` script, and the\n728\t   `node_modules/.cache/roast-diff` convention, and its CI job.\n729\t6. `package.json` to its 2.1 form (drops `workspaces`,\n730\t   `optionalDependencies`, `devEngines`, `build:launcher`, `release`,\n731\t   `test:ts`, `bundle`; `lint` loses its `--ignore-pattern` flags).\n732\t   `tsconfig.json` loses its legacy `exclude`. `.npmrc` to 2.2.\n733\t7. `.gitignore` per 2.2. Delete the generated root `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/`\n734\t   directory if present.\n735\t8. `ci.yml` to its 2.12 form; delete `.github/tools/staticcheck`,\n736\t   `.github/tools/govulncheck`, `.github/tools/licenses`.\n737\t   `renovate.json` keeps its `gomod` rules, which still match the\n738\t   remaining `.github/tools/*` modules.\n739\t9. `AGENTS.md`:\n740\t   - replace \"Go conventions\" with \"TypeScript conventions\": `npm run\n741\t     lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`; erasable syntax only in\n742\t     `scripts/`; `.js` relative imports in `src/` and `test/`; no\n743\t     `dependencies`; the test-env clearing helper and its provider list\n744\t     (successor of `ClearAmbientEnvironment` / `clearProviderEnv`);\n745\t   - rewrite \"npm packaging\" to describe 2.1 to 2.11 in short: bundle,\n746\t     notices, schema hook, test bundle, check:pack, release lifecycle,\n747\t     \"build before `npx roast`\";\n748\t   - in every other section, replace `internal/...` paths, `.go` files,\n749\t     and Go test helper names with the TS module paths and helper names\n750\t     each area file defines; drop the `GOFLAGS=-race`, `go mod tidy`,\n751\t     staticcheck, and `go list -deps` notes.\n752\t10. `README.md`: Quick start says Node 22.18 or later, macOS and Linux\n753\t    only, pure JavaScript (no prebuilt binaries, no Go toolchain);\n754\t    install text no longer mentions platform packages; a Network note\n755\t    documents `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1` and `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`.\n756\t    `--version` still\n757\t    prints version, commit, and build date.\n758\t11. `CONTRIBUTING.md`: prerequisites (Node 22.18+, Git; Go only to run\n759\t    the CI tool modules locally), commands (`npm run lint`,\n760\t    `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run build`), live tests via\n761\t    `npm run test:live` with the same `ROAST_LIVE_*` table, the release\n762\t    flow of 2.11, and third-party notices from 2.6. Remove the gofmt,\n763\t    `go mod tidy`, staticcheck, govulncheck, and `licenses.sh` text.\n764\t12. Update `.github/claude-review-prompt.md`: it frames the reviewer as\n765\t    a Go engineer; reword it for TypeScript. The workflow itself is\n766\t    unchanged.\n767\t13. Release: `npm version 2.0.0` on `main`.\n768\t14. After the release, deprecate the six `0.0.0`\n769\t    `@substrate-system/roast-<platform>-<arch>` packages on npm\n770\t    (`npm deprecate`), with a message pointing to\n771\t    `@substrate-system/roast` `2.0.0`.\n772\t\n773\t### 2.16 Runtime startup (`src/cli.ts`)\n774\t\n775\tBefore anything else runs, `src/cli.ts`:\n776\t\n777\t1. Checks `process.versions.node` against the floor `22.18.0`. Below it,\n778\t   the CLI writes a one-line error naming the required and the running\n779\t   version to stderr and exits non-zero without loading the rest of the\n780\t   bundle (`engines` only warns at install time, and an older Node would\n781\t   fail later with an obscure error). The check uses only syntax and\n782\t   APIs that every Node version able to parse the bundle supports.\n783\t2. Installs a `process.on('warning')` filter that drops only the\n784\t   `node:zlib` zstd `ExperimentalWarning`; every other warning is\n785\t   printed as Node would.\n786\t\n787\tThe README documents `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1` (Node's `fetch` ignores proxy\n788\tvariables without it) and `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS` for corporate proxies and\n789\tprivate CAs. No proxy library is bundled (spec.md, \"Network\").\n790\t\n791\t## 3. TypeScript module design\n792\t\n793\tRuntime code (bundled into `dist/cli.js`):\n794\t\n795\t- `src/cli.ts` -- bundle entry. No logic: calls the CLI area's\n796\t  `run(argv, io)` with `process.argv.slice(2)` and the real process IO,\n797\t  then sets `process.exitCode`. Importing `run` from elsewhere (tests)\n798\t  must not execute anything, so `run` lives in the CLI area's module, not\n799\t  here.\n800\t- `src/buildinfo.ts`:\n801\t\n802\t  ```ts\n803\t  export interface BuildInfo {\n804\t      version:string;\n805\t      commit:string;\n806\t      date:string;\n807\t  }\n808\t  export const buildInfo:BuildInfo\n809\t  export function formatBuildInfo (info:BuildInfo):string\n810\t  ```\n811\t\n812\t  Reads the three `__ROAST_*__` defines with a `typeof` guard so an\n813\t  unbundled or define-less build gets the sentinels (2.8).\n814\t- `src/assets.d.ts` -- ambient declarations (2.3).\n815\t\n816\tTooling (Node-run with type stripping, erasable syntax only):\n817\t\n818\t- `scripts/bundle.ts` -- entry. Modes: default (the bundle, 2.5),\n819\t  `--test`, `--live`, `--diff` (until M6). Imports `esbuild` and\n820\t  `scripts/licenses.ts`. Has no exports.\n821\t- `scripts/licenses.ts` -- pure library, no top-level side effects, so the\n822\t  test bundle can import it:\n823\t\n824\t  ```ts\n825\t  import type { Metafile } from 'esbuild'\n826\t\n827\t  export const ALLOWED_LICENSES:readonly string[]\n828\t  export interface BundledPackage {\n829\t      name:string;\n830\t      version:string;\n831\t      license:string;\n832\t      repository:string|null;\n833\t      dir:string;\n834\t      licenseFiles:string[];\n835\t  }\n836\t  export function bundledPackageDirs (\n837\t      metafile:Metafile,\n838\t      outfile:string\n839\t  ):string[]\n840\t  export function readBundledPackages (dirs:string[]):BundledPackage[]\n841\t  export function renderNotices (\n842\t      packages:BundledPackage[],\n843\t      readFile:(path:string) => string\n844\t  ):string\n845\t  ```\n846\t\n847\t  `readBundledPackages` throws an `Error` naming the package on any 2.6\n848\t  validation failure.\n849\t- `scripts/schema.ts` -- entry (2.7). Depends on the config area's\n850\t  `src/config/json-schema.ts` (`renderProjectSchema():string`).\n851\t- `scripts/check-pack.ts` -- entry (2.10). Named `check-package.ts` until\n852\t  M6.\n853\t\n854\tTests:\n855\t\n856\t- `test/index.ts` -- the single test entry; imports `test/tooling/*.ts`\n857\t  and each area's `test/<area>/*.ts`.\n858\t- `test/tooling/` -- this area's tests (section 5).\n859\t- `test/live/index.ts` -- live-test entry (owned by the LLM area).\n860\t- `test/diff/` -- the differential harness (until M6). It reuses the fake\n861\t  inference server from the CLI test helpers rather than defining its own.\n862\t\n863\tDependencies on other areas: the CLI area (`run`, `.locale('en')` /\n864\t`.detectLocale(false)`), the config area (`renderProjectSchema`), the\n865\tprompts, skill, and gate areas (text asset imports), and the LLM, doctor,\n866\tand record areas (consumers of `buildInfo`).\n867\t\n868\t## 4. Deliberate changes\n869\t\n870\tFrom `00-decisions.md`, the ones that touch this area:\n871\t\n872\t1. Windows is not supported: no `win32` packages, `\"os\": [\"darwin\",\n873\t   \"linux\"]`, and the test pipeline may use `bash`.\n874\t2. `engines.node` is `>=22.18` (the baseline said `>=20`, with a\n875\t   `devEngines` of `>=22.18`).\n876\t3. First TS release is `2.0.0`.\n877\t4. `@substrate-system/debug` is bundled as a runtime library.\n878\t5. Packaging: one pure-JS package with a bundled `dist/cli.js` replaces\n879\t   the root launcher plus six platform packages; the template npm\n880\t   lifecycle replaces the release scripts; `check:pack` is slimmed; CI\n881\t   becomes lint, typecheck, test, check:pack on Ubuntu and macOS with\n882\t   Node 22 and 24.\n883\t\n884\tConsequences for build info: the Go fallback to toolchain VCS stamps is\n885\tdropped (2.8). Consequences for CI: `govulncheck`, `go-licenses`, vet,\n886\tstaticcheck, gofmt, and the race detector have no successors other than\n887\tthe 2.6 license allowlist and `tsc` plus eslint.\n888\t\n889\t## 5. Test plan\n890\t\n891\tAll tests here are tapzero tests in `test/tooling/`, run from the test\n892\tbundle. Assertions are on exit codes, files, and parsed data, never on\n893\thuman-readable wording.\n894\t\n895\t### 5.1 Bundle smoke tests (spawn `node dist/cli.js`)\n896\t\n897\t- `--version` exits 0 and its stdout contains the `package.json`\n898\t  version.\n899\t- `--help` exits 0; its stdout under `LC_ALL=de_DE.UTF-8\n900\t  LANG=de_DE.UTF-8` equals its stdout under `LC_ALL=C` (locale pinned,\n901\t  2.5 caveat).\n902\t- In a temporary Git repository with a toplevel `.roast.json` containing\n903\t  comments and a `gate` section, `gate settings` exits 0 and prints\n904\t  `timeout_seconds=` and `severity=` lines with the configured values\n905\t  (bundled `jsonc-parser` and `zod` work).\n906\t- `dist/cli.js` starts with `#!/usr/bin/env node` and has the owner\n907\t  execute bit.\n908\t\n909\t- With a Node version below 22.18 reported (the startup check takes the\n910\t  version as an argument), the check returns an error naming `22.18` and\n911\t  the CLI exits non-zero; at or above the floor it passes.\n912\t- The zstd `ExperimentalWarning` filter drops that warning and passes\n913\t  other warnings through.\n914\t\n915\t### 5.2 Assets and build info\n916\t\n917\t- Each text asset imported through the loader equals the file read from\n918\t  disk (12 prompt templates, `SKILL.md`, `pre-commit.sh`).\n919\t- `formatBuildInfo` uses the `(commit <c>)` form when the version is\n920\t  `dev` or the date is `unknown`, and the `(<c>, <d>)` form otherwise\n921\t  (Go `TestResolve` covers only the toolchain fallback, which is dropped).\n922\t- In the test bundle `buildInfo.version` is `dev`.\n923\t\n924\t### 5.3 Third-party notices\n925\t\n926\tUsing a fixture `node_modules` in a temp directory and a hand-built\n927\tmetafile:\n928\t\n929\t- collects unscoped, scoped, and nested-`node_modules` packages, and\n930\t  deduplicates by `name@version`;\n931\t- ignores inputs with `bytesInOutput: 0` and inputs outside\n932\t  `node_modules`;\n933\t- rejects a package with no license file, no `license` field, or a\n934\t  license outside the allowlist, naming the package;\n935\t- renders packages sorted by name then version, deterministically (two\n936\t  renders are equal).\n937\t\n938\tAgainst the real build: every package derived from `dist/meta.json`\n939\tappears as a `<name>@<version>` header line in\n940\t`dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`.\n941\t\n942\t(Provenance: `TestLicenseGenerationGuards`,\n943\t`TestLicenseBundleGeneration`; the ownership-marker test\n944\t`TestLicenseBundleOwnershipSurvivesToolUpdates` has no successor because\n945\tnotices are a single generated file under `dist/`.)\n946\t\n947\t### 5.4 Package check\n948\t\n949\tRuns the real `scripts/check-pack.ts` (`check-package.ts` until M6) with\n950\t`cwd` set to a fixture package that copies the real `files` and\n951\t`license` from the repo `package.json` and holds stub files:\n952\t\n953\t- passes when every required file is present;\n954\t- fails when the tarball lacks `dist/cli.js`\n955\t  (\"fails when the root tarball lacks the launcher\");\n956\t- fails when it lacks `roast.schema.json`\n957\t  (\"fails when the root tarball lacks the schema\");\n958\t- fails when it lacks one of Roast's own license files\n959\t  (\"fails when the root tarball lacks Roast's own license\");\n960\t- fails when it lacks `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`\n961\t  (\"fails when a platform tarball lacks license notices\");\n962\t- fails when the manifest declares no license\n963\t  (\"fails when a packed manifest declares no license\");\n964\t- fails when the manifest declares `dependencies` or\n965\t  `optionalDependencies` (\"installing the root package pulls in only the\n966\t  platform packages\", `test/manifest.test.ts`);\n967\t- fails when `dist/cli.js` has no shebang or is not executable.\n968\t\n969\tTests that existed only for platform packages have no successor: launcher\n970\targument and exit-code passthrough and missing-package message\n971\t(`test/launcher.test.ts`), platform binary checks in check:pack, release\n972\tordering and abort (`test/release.test.ts`), version sync\n973\t(`test/version.test.ts`), prepublish version and binary checks\n974\t(`test/prepublish.test.ts`). The npm lifecycle itself is npm's behavior\n975\tand is not tested.\n976\t\n977\t### 5.5 Schema\n978\t\n979\tOwned by the config area: generated schema text equals the committed\n980\t`roast.schema.json` (successor of `TestSchemaMatchesConfigStruct`). The\n981\tinit area keeps \"the `$schema` written by init points inside\n982\t`node_modules/@substrate-system/roast/` at a `.json` file\"\n983\t(`TestInitSchemaPointsIntoTheInstalledPackage`).\n984\t\n985\t### 5.6 Differential harness\n986\t\n987\tScenario list and comparisons in 2.13. The harness is itself a test\n988\tsuite; it is not tested.\n989\t\n990\t## 6. Go baseline references\n991\t\n992\tAt commit `cd08f10`:\n993\t\n994\t- `package.json`, `.npmrc`, `tsconfig.json`, `.gitignore`,\n995\t  `renovate.json`\n996\t- `scripts/build.ts`, `scripts/check-pack.ts`, `scripts/check-release.ts`,\n997\t  `scripts/platforms.ts`, `scripts/release.ts`, `scripts/version.ts`,\n998\t  `scripts/licenses.sh`, `scripts/licenses_test.go`\n999\t- `src/launcher.ts`\n1000\t- `test/check-pack.test.ts`, `test/launcher.test.ts`,\n1001\t  `test/manifest.test.ts`, `test/prepublish.test.ts`,\n1002\t  `test/release.test.ts`, `test/version.test.ts`,\n1003\t  `test/release-fixture.ts`\n1004\t- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/tools/*`\n1005\t- `internal/buildinfo/buildinfo.go`, `internal/buildinfo/buildinfo_test.go`\n1006\t- `internal/config/schema_test.go` (`TestSchemaMatchesConfigStruct`)\n1007\t- `internal/cli/init_test.go`\n1008\t  (`TestInitSchemaPointsIntoTheInstalledPackage`)\n1009\t- `internal/prompts/prompts.go`, `internal/skill/skill.go`,\n1010\t  `internal/gate/gate.go` (`//go:embed` assets)\n1011\t- `AGENTS.md` (\"Go conventions\", \"npm packaging\"), `CONTRIBUTING.md`,\n1012\t  `README.md` (Quick start)\n1013\t- Template: `../template-ts-browser/` `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`,\n1014\t  `tsconfig.build.json`, `eslint.config.js`, `.npmrc`, `.npmignore`,\n1015\t  `test/index.ts`\n1016\t\n1017\t## 7. Resolved\n1018\t\n1019\t1. Keep the existing CHANGELOG history; auto-changelog regenerates new\n1020\t   entries from git tags (spec.md, \"Milestones\").\n1021\t2. CI macOS runner is `macos-latest` (2.12).\n1022\t3. CI adds an `npm audit` step covering the bundled devDependencies\n1023\t   (2.12).\n1024\t4. CI adds a `shellcheck` step for `pre-commit.sh` (2.12).\n1025\t5. `claude-review-prompt.md` is updated at M6 (2.15, item 12).\n1026\t6. The six `0.0.0` platform packages are deprecated on npm at M6 (2.15,\n1027\t   item 14).\n1028\t7. `@substrate-system/debug` and its dependencies are checked against the\n1029\t   license allowlist in M0 (2.14, item 11; spec.md, \"Further Notes\").\n1030\t8. `@types/yargs` is added to `devDependencies` (2.1).\n1031\t9. The differential harness runs in CI on Ubuntu only, M1 to M5, with an\n1032\t   allowlist of spec.md's deliberate changes; deleted at M6 (2.13;\n1033\t   spec.md, \"Testing Decisions\").\n1034\t10. The CLI checks the Node version at startup and errors clearly below\n1035\t    22.18 (2.16; spec.md, decision 3).\n1036\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"453ecfdf-dc0d-4287-be41-1cc75a67a074","uuid":"8db037ca-f92b-425e-bee6-5b1cb50f4627","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:02:43.871Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-01-m0-scaffold/.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/15-packaging.md","content":"  (gitleaks through `.github/tools/gitleaks/go.mod`) and workflow lint\n  (actionlint through `.github/tools/actionlint/go.mod`). It adds two\n  steps: `npm audit --audit-level=high`, run after the install step\n  (without `--omit=dev`, so the bundled runtime libraries, which are\n  `devDependencies`, are covered), and `shellcheck\n  src/gate/pre-commit.sh` (the hook script is the only shell file left).\n  `setup-go` stays\n  only for these tool modules, with `go-version-file` pointing at the\n  tool's own `go.mod` and `cache-dependency-path: .github/tools/*/go.sum`.\n  The tool modules' `go mod tidy` check stays, limited to `.github/tools`.\n\nBaseline steps removed at M6: Set up Go in the test job, `go mod\ndownload`, gofmt check, root `go mod tidy` check, `shellcheck\nscripts/*.sh` (replaced by the hook-script step above), `GOFLAGS: -race`\non Test, `go vet`,\nstaticcheck, \"Build all platform packages\", govulncheck, `go-licenses\ncheck` (replaced by the allowlist in 2.6), and `bash scripts/licenses.sh`.\nTool modules deleted with them: `.github/tools/staticcheck`,\n`.github/tools/govulncheck`, `.github/tools/licenses`.\n\nDuring M0 to M5, `ci.yml` keeps every baseline job and adds the job\n`typescript` (2.14) and the differential harness job (2.13).\n\n### 2.13 Go-vs-TS differential harness (temporary)\n\nPurpose: prove parity on observable output by running the baseline Go CLI\nand the TS CLI on identical inputs against the same fake inference server.\nIt lives in `test/diff/` with entry `test/diff/index.ts`, bundled to\n`test/diff-bundle.js` by `scripts/bundle.ts --diff`, run by\n`npm run test:diff`. It is not imported by `test/index.ts` and is deleted\nat M6.\n\nCI runs it from M1 to M5 on Ubuntu only (a job in `ci.yml` with Go set\nup, then `npm run build` and `npm run test:diff`), with an allowlist of\nthe deliberate changes listed in spec.md, \"Deliberate changes from the Go\nbaseline\". Differences outside the allowlist fail the job.\n\nBuilding the Go baseline:\n\n1. Binary cache path: `node_modules/.cache/roast-diff/roast-go-cd08f10`.\n   Reuse it if present.\n2. Otherwise: `git worktree add --detach <tmp>/roast-go cd08f10`, then in\n   it `go build -trimpath -ldflags \"-X\n   github.com/bluesky-social/roast/internal/buildinfo.Version=baseline\" -o\n   <cache path> ./cmd/roast` with `CGO_ENABLED=0` and `GOFLAGS` removed\n   from the environment, then `git worktree remove --force <tmp>/roast-go`\n   (also on failure).\n3. If `go` is not on `PATH`, the harness prints a TAP skip for every\n   scenario and exits 0 (CI installs Go, so it never skips there).\n\nThe TS side is `dist/cli.js` (the harness requires `npm run build` first),\nspawned as `node dist/cli.js`, not the in-process `run`, so both CLIs are\nexercised as processes.\n\nPer scenario:\n\n1. Start one `node:http` fake server (the same fake the CLI tests use,\n   speaking the `chat`, `responses`, and `anthropic` protocols). Responses\n   are scripted per scenario and selected by request content (model name\n   plus number of conversation turns), never by arrival order, because\n   finder and verifier calls may interleave differently.\n2. Build two identical fixture repositories, one per CLI, from the same\n   function: fixed file contents, fixed `GIT_AUTHOR_DATE` /\n   `GIT_COMMITTER_DATE` and identity, so commit IDs match.\n3. Write the same `.roast.json` (profiles on the fake's URL, credentials\n   via `api_key_env`) into both. Each CLI approves its own copy with\n   `trust --yes` first: trust hashes differ by design (v1 vs v2).\n4. Run each CLI with a scrubbed environment: no `ROAST_*`, `OPENAI_*`,\n   `OPENROUTER_*`, `ANTHROPIC_*`, `DEBUG`; private `HOME` and\n   `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`; the profile's key variable set.\n5. Compare, after normalization:\n   - exit code (exact);\n   - stdout when the scenario requests JSON output (parsed, deep equal);\n   - requests the fake received, grouped by (model, turn count): method,\n     path, parsed JSON body deep equal, and header names (values compared\n     only for `Content-Type` and the auth scheme). This covers the\n     rendered `finder_user` / `verifier_user` prompts, which reach the\n     fake verbatim;\n   - run records: the set of relative file paths in the run directory;\n     every JSON and JSONL file parsed and deep equal; raw response\n     captures byte equal; run bundles compared as decompressed tar entries\n     (name, mode, size, content), not compressed bytes, because the zstd\n     encoders differ.\n   Normalization replaces run IDs, timestamps, durations, the fixture\n   repository path, `roast.version` / `roast.commit`, the `User-Agent`\n   value, and session header values with placeholders.\n6. Not compared: stderr, rendered Markdown, help text, and anything\n   touched by a deliberate change (trust messages and `trust.json`, the\n   `completion` command, debug output).\n\nScenarios are added per milestone (M1: config errors and `gate settings`;\nM3: clean review, review with findings, `--json`, `--staged`,\n`--max-severity`, a failing provider; M4: the same review scenarios on\n`responses` and `anthropic`; M5: `runs` listing and snapshot commands,\n`init` with a fake provider). A scenario that fails because Go behavior\nwas judged wrong is recorded in the owning area's Open questions, not\npatched in the harness.\n\n### 2.14 M0 scaffold\n\nM0 lets the other areas land TS code and tests while the Go build, the\nlauncher, and the platform release flow keep working unchanged. Contents:\n\n1. `package.json`: add the `devDependencies` from 2.1 (keeping the\n   baseline ones, and moving `jsonc-parser`, `yargs`, `zod` out of\n   `dependencies`); add scripts `lint`, `typecheck`, `bundle`\n   (`node scripts/bundle.ts`), `build:test`, `test:tap`, `test:ts`\n   (`npm run bundle && npm run build:test && npm run test:tap`),\n   `test:diff` (`npm run bundle && node scripts/bundle.ts --diff &&\n   node test/diff-bundle.js`). `build`, `build:launcher`, `test`, `version`,\n   `prepublishOnly`, `check:pack`, `release` keep their baseline meaning.\n   `bin`, `files`, `workspaces`, `engines`, `optionalDependencies` are\n   untouched.\n2. The transitional `lint` script:\n   `eslint src test scripts eslint.config.js` plus one `--ignore-pattern`\n   per legacy file: `src/launcher.ts`, `test/*.test.ts`,\n   `test/release-fixture.ts`, `scripts/build.ts`, `scripts/check-pack.ts`,\n   `scripts/check-release.ts`, `scripts/platforms.ts`,\n   `scripts/release.ts`, `scripts/version.ts`.\n3. TypeScript: `tsconfig.json` becomes 2.3's file plus `exclude` of the\n   same legacy files; `tsconfig.build.json` as in 2.3. The launcher's\n   current config moves to `tsconfig.launcher.json` and `build:launcher`\n   becomes `tsc -p tsconfig.launcher.json`.\n4. `eslint.config.js` copied from the template (2.4).\n5. New tooling: `scripts/bundle.ts` (with `--test`, `--live`, `--diff`),\n   `scripts/licenses.ts`. `scripts/schema.ts` lands in M1. The slimmed\n   package check is written as `scripts/check-package.ts` (it would fail\n   against the transitional manifest, so CI does not run it yet; its\n   fixture tests do run); M6 renames it to `scripts/check-pack.ts` over\n   the old one.\n6. Source: `src/cli.ts` (the bundle entry; it only hands\n   `process.argv.slice(2)` and the real process IO to the CLI area's\n   `run` and sets `process.exitCode` from its result; in M0 `run` handles\n   `--version` only), `src/buildinfo.ts`, `src/assets.d.ts`.\n7. Tests: `test/index.ts` importing `test/tooling/*.ts` (5.1 to 5.4).\n8. `.gitignore`: add `test/*.js`.\n9. CI: new job `typescript` in `ci.yml` with the 2.12 matrix and steps\n   checkout, setup-node, install, `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`,\n   `npm run test:ts`. The baseline `quality` and `security` jobs are\n   unchanged until M6.\n10. `.npmrc` keeps `force=true` until M6 (the workspaces still exist).\n11. License check: `@substrate-system/debug` and every dependency it\n    pulls into the bundle must pass the 2.6 allowlist. M0 runs the\n    bundle with the license step against them and resolves any failure\n    (replace the library or extend the allowlist with maintainer\n    approval) before other areas depend on it.\n\n### 2.15 M6 cutover checklist\n\nPreconditions: every area's test plan is ported and green; the\ndifferential harness passes every scenario (or each difference is an\naccepted Open question); `npm run build && npm run check:pack` passes\nagainst the final manifest in a scratch commit.\n\n1. Move assets with `git mv` (list in 2.5) and update their imports.\n2. Delete Go: `cmd/`, `internal/`, `go.mod`, `go.sum`.\n3. Delete npm-packaging code: `packages/`, `src/launcher.ts`,\n   `tsconfig.launcher.json`, `scripts/build.ts`, the old\n   `scripts/check-pack.ts`, `scripts/check-release.ts`,\n   `scripts/platforms.ts`, `scripts/release.ts`, `scripts/version.ts`,\n   `scripts/licenses.sh`, `scripts/licenses_test.go`, and their tests\n   `test/launcher.test.ts`, `test/manifest.test.ts`,\n   `test/check-pack.test.ts`, `test/prepublish.test.ts`,\n   `test/release.test.ts`, `test/version.test.ts`,\n   `test/release-fixture.ts`.\n4. Rename `scripts/check-package.ts` to `scripts/check-pack.ts`.\n5. Delete the differential harness: `test/diff/`, the `--diff` mode of\n   `scripts/bundle.ts`, the `test:diff` script, and the\n   `node_modules/.cache/roast-diff` convention, and its CI job.\n6. `package.json` to its 2.1 form (drops `workspaces`,\n   `optionalDependencies`, `devEngines`, `build:launcher`, `release`,\n   `test:ts`, `bundle`; `lint` loses its `--ignore-pattern` flags).\n   `tsconfig.json` loses its legacy `exclude`. `.npmrc` to 2.2.\n7. `.gitignore` per 2.2. Delete the generated root `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/`\n   directory if present.\n8. `ci.yml` to its 2.12 form; delete `.github/tools/staticcheck`,\n   `.github/tools/govulncheck`, `.github/tools/licenses`.\n   `renovate.json` keeps its `gomod` rules, which still match the\n   remaining `.github/tools/*` modules.\n9. `AGENTS.md`:\n   - replace \"Go conventions\" with \"TypeScript conventions\": `npm run\n     lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`; erasable syntax only in\n     `scripts/`; `.js` relative imports in `src/` and `test/`; no\n     `dependencies`; the test-env clearing helper and its provider list\n     (successor of `ClearAmbientEnvironment` / `clearProviderEnv`);\n   - rewrite \"npm packaging\" to describe 2.1 to 2.11 in short: bundle,\n     notices, schema hook, test bundle, check:pack, release lifecycle,\n     \"build before `npx roast`\";\n   - in every other section, replace `internal/...` paths, `.go` files,\n     and Go test helper names with the TS module paths and helper names\n     each area file defines; drop the `GOFLAGS=-race`, `go mod tidy`,\n     staticcheck, and `go list -deps` notes.\n10. `README.md`: Quick start says Node 22.18 or later, macOS and Linux\n    only, pure JavaScript (no prebuilt binaries, no Go toolchain);\n    install text no longer mentions platform packages; a Network note\n    documents `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1` and `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`.\n    `--version` still\n    prints version, commit, and build date.\n11. `CONTRIBUTING.md`: prerequisites (Node 22.18+, Git; Go only to run\n    the CI tool modules locally), commands (`npm run lint`,\n    `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run build`), live tests via\n    `npm run test:live` with the same `ROAST_LIVE_*` table, the release\n    flow of 2.11, and third-party notices from 2.6. Remove the gofmt,\n    `go mod tidy`, staticcheck, govulncheck, and `licenses.sh` text.\n12. Update `.github/claude-review-prompt.md`: it frames the reviewer as\n    a Go engineer; reword it for TypeScript. The workflow itself is\n    unchanged.\n13. Release: `npm version 2.0.0` on `main`.\n14. After the release, deprecate the six `0.0.0`\n    `@substrate-system/roast-<platform>-<arch>` packages on npm\n    (`npm deprecate`), with a message pointing to\n    `@substrate-system/roast` `2.0.0`.\n\n### 2.16 Runtime startup (`src/cli.ts`)\n\nBefore anything else runs, `src/cli.ts`:\n\n1. Checks `process.versions.node` against the floor `22.18.0`. Below it,\n   the CLI writes a one-line error naming the required and the running\n   version to stderr and exits non-zero without loading the rest of the\n   bundle (`engines` only warns at install time, and an older Node would\n   fail later with an obscure error). The check uses only syntax and\n   APIs that every Node version able to parse the bundle supports.\n2. Installs a `process.on('warning')` filter that drops only the\n   `node:zlib` zstd `ExperimentalWarning`; every other warning is\n   printed as Node would.\n\nThe README documents `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1` (Node's `fetch` ignores proxy\nvariables without it) and `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS` for corporate proxies and\nprivate CAs. No proxy library is bundled (spec.md, \"Network\").\n\n## 3. TypeScript module design\n\nRuntime code (bundled into `dist/cli.js`):\n\n- `src/cli.ts` -- bundle entry. No logic: calls the CLI area's\n  `run(argv, io)` with `process.argv.slice(2)` and the real process IO,\n  then sets `process.exitCode`. Importing `run` from elsewhere (tests)\n  must not execute anything, so `run` lives in the CLI area's module, not\n  here.\n- `src/buildinfo.ts`:\n\n  ```ts\n  export interface BuildInfo {\n      version:string;\n      commit:string;\n      date:string;\n  }\n  export const buildInfo:BuildInfo\n  export function formatBuildInfo (info:BuildInfo):string\n  ```\n\n  Reads the three `__ROAST_*__` defines with a `typeof` guard so an\n  unbundled or define-less build gets the sentinels (2.8).\n- `src/assets.d.ts` -- ambient declarations (2.3).\n\nTooling (Node-run with type stripping, erasable syntax only):\n\n- `scripts/bundle.ts` -- entry. Modes: default (the bundle, 2.5),\n  `--test`, `--live`, `--diff` (until M6). Imports `esbuild` and\n  `scripts/licenses.ts`. Has no exports.\n- `scripts/licenses.ts` -- pure library, no top-level side effects, so the\n  test bundle can import it:\n\n  ```ts\n  import type { Metafile } from 'esbuild'\n\n  export const ALLOWED_LICENSES:readonly string[]\n  export interface BundledPackage {\n      name:string;\n      version:string;\n      license:string;\n      repository:string|null;\n      dir:string;\n      licenseFiles:string[];\n  }\n  export function bundledPackageDirs (\n      metafile:Metafile,\n      outfile:string\n  ):string[]\n  export function readBundledPackages (dirs:string[]):BundledPackage[]\n  export function renderNotices (\n      packages:BundledPackage[],\n      readFile:(path:string) => string\n  ):string\n  ```\n\n  `readBundledPackages` throws an `Error` naming the package on any 2.6\n  validation failure.\n- `scripts/schema.ts` -- entry (2.7). Depends on the config area's\n  `src/config/json-schema.ts` (`renderProjectSchema():string`).\n- `scripts/check-pack.ts` -- entry (2.10). Named `check-package.ts` until\n  M6.\n\nTests:\n\n- `test/index.ts` -- the single test entry; imports `test/tooling/*.ts`\n  and each area's `test/<area>/*.ts`.\n- `test/tooling/` -- this area's tests (section 5).\n- `test/live/index.ts` -- live-test entry (owned by the LLM area).\n- `test/diff/` -- the differential harness (until M6). It reuses the fake\n  inference server from the CLI test helpers rather than defining its own.\n\nDependencies on other areas: the CLI area (`run`, `.locale('en')` /\n`.detectLocale(false)`), the config area (`renderProjectSchema`), the\nprompts, skill, and gate areas (text asset imports), and the LLM, doctor,\nand record areas (consumers of `buildInfo`).\n\n## 4. Deliberate changes\n\nFrom `00-decisions.md`, the ones that touch this area:\n\n1. Windows is not supported: no `win32` packages, `\"os\": [\"darwin\",\n   \"linux\"]`, and the test pipeline may use `bash`.\n2. `engines.node` is `>=22.18` (the baseline said `>=20`, with a\n   `devEngines` of `>=22.18`).\n3. First TS release is `2.0.0`.\n4. `@substrate-system/debug` is bundled as a runtime library.\n5. Packaging: one pure-JS package with a bundled `dist/cli.js` replaces\n   the root launcher plus six platform packages; the template npm\n   lifecycle replaces the release scripts; `check:pack` is slimmed; CI\n   becomes lint, typecheck, test, check:pack on Ubuntu and macOS with\n   Node 22 and 24.\n\nConsequences for build info: the Go fallback to toolchain VCS stamps is\ndropped (2.8). Consequences for CI: `govulncheck`, `go-licenses`, vet,\nstaticcheck, gofmt, and the race detector have no successors other than\nthe 2.6 license allowlist and `tsc` plus eslint.\n\n## 5. Test plan\n\nAll tests here are tapzero tests in `test/tooling/`, run from the test\nbundle. Assertions are on exit codes, files, and parsed data, never on\nhuman-readable wording.\n\n### 5.1 Bundle smoke tests (spawn `node dist/cli.js`)\n\n- `--version` exits 0 and its stdout contains the `package.json`\n  version.\n- `--help` exits 0; its stdout under `LC_ALL=de_DE.UTF-8\n  LANG=de_DE.UTF-8` equals its stdout under `LC_ALL=C` (locale pinned,\n  2.5 caveat).\n- In a temporary Git repository with a toplevel `.roast.json` containing\n  comments and a `gate` section, `gate settings` exits 0 and prints\n  `timeout_seconds=` and `severity=` lines with the configured values\n  (bundled `jsonc-parser` and `zod` work).\n- `dist/cli.js` starts with `#!/usr/bin/env node` and has the owner\n  execute bit.\n\n- With a Node version below 22.18 reported (the startup check takes the\n  version as an argument), the check returns an error naming `22.18` and\n  the CLI exits non-zero; at or above the floor it passes.\n- The zstd `ExperimentalWarning` filter drops that warning and passes\n  other warnings through.\n\n### 5.2 Assets and build info\n\n- Each text asset imported through the loader equals the file read from\n  disk (12 prompt templates, `SKILL.md`, `pre-commit.sh`).\n- `formatBuildInfo` uses the `(commit <c>)` form when the version is\n  `dev` or the date is `unknown`, and the `(<c>, <d>)` form otherwise\n  (Go `TestResolve` covers only the toolchain fallback, which is dropped).\n- In the test bundle `buildInfo.version` is `dev`.\n\n### 5.3 Third-party notices\n\nUsing a fixture `node_modules` in a temp directory and a hand-built\nmetafile:\n\n- collects unscoped, scoped, and nested-`node_modules` packages, and\n  deduplicates by `name@version`;\n- ignores inputs with `bytesInOutput: 0` and inputs outside\n  `node_modules`;\n- rejects a package with no license file, no `license` field, or a\n  license outside the allowlist, naming the package;\n- renders packages sorted by name then version, deterministically (two\n  renders are equal).\n\nAgainst the real build: every package derived from `dist/meta.json`\nappears as a `<name>@<version>` header line in\n`dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`.\n\n(Provenance: `TestLicenseGenerationGuards`,\n`TestLicenseBundleGeneration`; the ownership-marker test\n`TestLicenseBundleOwnershipSurvivesToolUpdates` has no successor because\nnotices are a single generated file under `dist/`.)\n\n### 5.4 Package check\n\nRuns the real `scripts/check-pack.ts` (`check-package.ts` until M6) with\n`cwd` set to a fixture package that copies the real `files` and\n`license` from the repo `package.json` and holds stub files:\n\n- passes when every required file is present;\n- fails when the tarball lacks `dist/cli.js`\n  (\"fails when the root tarball lacks the launcher\");\n- fails when it lacks `roast.schema.json`\n  (\"fails when the root tarball lacks the schema\");\n- fails when it lacks one of Roast's own license files\n  (\"fails when the root tarball lacks Roast's own license\");\n- fails when it lacks `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`\n  (\"fails when a platform tarball lacks license notices\");\n- fails when the manifest declares no license\n  (\"fails when a packed manifest declares no license\");\n- fails when the manifest declares `dependencies` or\n  `optionalDependencies` (\"installing the root package pulls in only the\n  platform packages\", `test/manifest.test.ts`);\n- fails when `dist/cli.js` has no shebang or is not executable.\n\nTests that existed only for platform packages have no successor: launcher\nargument and exit-code passthrough and missing-package message\n(`test/launcher.test.ts`), platform binary checks in check:pack, release\nordering and abort (`test/release.test.ts`), version sync\n(`test/version.test.ts`), prepublish version and binary checks\n(`test/prepublish.test.ts`). The npm lifecycle itself is npm's behavior\nand is not tested.\n\n### 5.5 Schema\n\nOwned by the config area: generated schema text equals the committed\n`roast.schema.json` (successor of `TestSchemaMatchesConfigStruct`). The\ninit area keeps \"the `$schema` written by init points inside\n`node_modules/@substrate-system/roast/` at a `.json` file\"\n(`TestInitSchemaPointsIntoTheInstalledPackage`).\n\n### 5.6 Differential harness\n\nScenario list and comparisons in 2.13. The harness is itself a test\nsuite; it is not tested.\n\n## 6. Go baseline references\n\nAt commit `cd08f10`:\n\n- `package.json`, `.npmrc`, `tsconfig.json`, `.gitignore`,\n  `renovate.json`\n- `scripts/build.ts`, `scripts/check-pack.ts`, `scripts/check-release.ts`,\n  `scripts/platforms.ts`, `scripts/release.ts`, `scripts/version.ts`,\n  `scripts/licenses.sh`, `scripts/licenses_test.go`\n- `src/launcher.ts`\n- `test/check-pack.test.ts`, `test/launcher.test.ts`,\n  `test/manifest.test.ts`, `test/prepublish.test.ts`,\n  `test/release.test.ts`, `test/version.test.ts`,\n  `test/release-fixture.ts`\n- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/tools/*`\n- `internal/buildinfo/buildinfo.go`, `internal/buildinfo/buildinfo_test.go`\n- `internal/config/schema_test.go` (`TestSchemaMatchesConfigStruct`)\n- `internal/cli/init_test.go`\n  (`TestInitSchemaPointsIntoTheInstalledPackage`)\n- `internal/prompts/prompts.go`, `internal/skill/skill.go`,\n  `internal/gate/gate.go` (`//go:embed` assets)\n- `AGENTS.md` (\"Go conventions\", \"npm packaging\"), `CONTRIBUTING.md`,\n  `README.md` (Quick start)\n- Template: `../template-ts-browser/` `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`,\n  `tsconfig.build.json`, `eslint.config.js`, `.npmrc`, `.npmignore`,\n  `test/index.ts`\n\n## 7. Resolved\n\n1. Keep the existing CHANGELOG history; auto-changelog regenerates new\n   entries from git tags (spec.md, \"Milestones\").\n2. CI macOS runner is `macos-latest` (2.12).\n3. CI adds an `npm audit` step covering the bundled devDependencies\n   (2.12).\n4. CI adds a `shellcheck` step for `pre-commit.sh` (2.12).\n5. `claude-review-prompt.md` is updated at M6 (2.15, item 12).\n6. The six `0.0.0` platform packages are deprecated on npm at M6 (2.15,\n   item 14).\n7. `@substrate-system/debug` and its dependencies are checked against the\n   license allowlist in M0 (2.14, item 11; spec.md, \"Further Notes\").\n8. `@types/yargs` is added to `devDependencies` (2.1).\n9. The differential harness runs in CI on Ubuntu only, M1 to M5, with an\n   allowlist of spec.md's deliberate changes; deleted at M6 (2.13;\n   spec.md, \"Testing Decisions\").\n10. The CLI checks the Node version at startup and errors clearly below\n    22.18 (2.16; spec.md, decision 3).\n","numLines":477,"startLine":560,"totalLines":1036}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018Bj7FMoWDHKwV6BC3PP6xy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
