{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAvWv2U9XmfCu6dj1WU9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test:ts` pass; `npm run build:launcher`, `go build ./...`, and `go test ./...` still pass.\n\nThe M0 scaffold is done and committed in six commits on `roast--ts-rewrite-01-m0-scaffold`. Every acceptance criterion has a passing test. `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck` and `npm run test:ts` (72 assertions) pass, and so do `npm run build:launcher`, `go build ./...` and the full `npm test` (Go tests plus launcher tests, exit 0).\n\n**What's in place**\n- **Package and config:** `package.json` has the new dev dependencies and scripts; `jsonc-parser`, `yargs` and `zod` moved to `devDependencies`, and `@types/node` is on 22. There are new `tsconfig.json`, `tsconfig.build.json` and `tsconfig.launcher.json` files, `eslint.config.js` copied byte for byte from the template, `test/*.js` in `.gitignore`, and a `typescript` CI job with the 2×2 matrix (actionlint passes).\n- **`scripts/bundle.ts`:** default, `--test` and `--live` modes. The empty `writeThirdPartyNotices(metafile)` function is the hook ticket 02 fills in.\n- **Source:** `src/cli.ts` is the entry. It checks the Node version, filters the zstd warning, then loads the CLI body. I checked `dist/cli.js` and that body is only initialized after the check. `src/cli/run.ts` handles `--version`/`-v` and `--help` with yargs pinned to English. Anything else exits 2 as not implemented yet. `src/buildinfo.ts` and `src/assets.d.ts` match the spec.\n- **Startup helpers:** the version check and warning filter live in a separate `src/startup.ts`, because importing `src/cli.ts` runs the CLI. The filter wraps Node's own warning printer, so other warnings print exactly as Node prints them and `--no-warnings` still prints nothing.\n\n**Decisions you should look at**\n1. **typescript-eslint refuses TypeScript 7**, which the spec pins (`^7.0.2`). npm `overrides` couldn't fix it. I didn't touch the eslint config. Instead I added the dev dependency `@typescript/typescript6` and a small hook, `scripts/eslint-ts6.ts`. The `lint` script loads that hook, so only the eslint process gets the TypeScript 6 API; `typecheck` still uses TypeScript 7. Remove the hook once typescript-eslint supports TypeScript 7.\n2. **`tap-spec` already exits 1 on `not ok` lines and on a missing plan.** Pipefail only matters when the TAP output looks complete and passing but the test bundle still exits non-zero. The tests cover exactly that case, and they fail if pipefail is removed from the script.\n3. **The \"importing `run.ts` does nothing\" test runs in a child process.** It bundles an entry that only imports `run.ts`, runs it, and expects no output and exit 0. An in-process check would quietly stop testing anything once another test imports `run.ts` directly.\n4. The first install failed on a stale npm cache entry (ETARGET). One `npm view` refreshed it, and the same install command then worked.\n\nReusable notes are now in `AGENTS.md` under \"TypeScript rewrite tooling\", and details of this attempt are in `.redeye/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":713,"cache_read_input_tokens":144016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":713},"output_tokens":822,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"453ecfdf-dc0d-4287-be41-1cc75a67a074","uuid":"6686a630-0689-4c54-baeb-d10c55e0f6f5","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:11:39.343Z","request_id":"req_011ChAvWup4bHqRRPxhp6tDS"}
